{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation","id":551489,"title":"Court Creation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-12T08:09:09-07:00","id":551489,"title":"Court Creation","content":"I just posted Court Creation and Toronto. This thread is for discussing Court Creation. <br /> <br /> This is the post: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-court-creation-and-toronto/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-th...n-and-toronto/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T08:39:20-07:00","id":551578,"title":"","content":"So, Let's toss an idea out there.<br /> <br /> Your base story is the tale as old as time, Beauty and the Beast, but it's <i>also</i> Little Red Riding Hood, the two used together to create dynamics and depth. They refer, in their way, to a basic story that's as old as Enkidu and Shamhat-the sacred woman(Hood/Belle) falling in love/lust with the carnal, worldly man(The Beast/The Wolf). Gender isn't actually important, both can be women or men or trans or whatever combo. On top of that, you have the dynamic of the Woodsman from Hood and Gaston/Avenant from Beauty as the beast, the Woodsman(Huntsman) alternatively cast as hero and villain, much like the beastly character.<br /> <br /> Build a Bulwark and Courts out of it.<br /> <br /> Yes, this is the idea I was playing with for the Paris Courts. I want to see if the ideas I have are going in a sane direction.<br /> <br /> EDIT: ALso, I'm just super curious about what people will come up with on this setup. I'll put out what I have so far once I see some ideas.<br /> <br /> BONUS POINTS: Incorporate dueling as a major mechanism.<br /> <br /> EXTRA BONUS POINTS: Build the Courts, not on the archetypes? but on responses to the Story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-12-2015, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T09:09:37-07:00","id":551652,"title":"","content":"I really like what I'm seeing just from my initial read through. I'm probably going to pick it apart later, but so far it looks great.<br /> <br /> One thing I love is that the example Court is such an odd concept. Rather than go with the more by the book stuff like Seasons or Day/Night (which it looks like will be covered in the locations section), the book gives you an idea of just how weird and creative you can get with it. &quot;A town's industries&quot; is <i>not</i> something I would have ever imagined as a Court structure, but dang if it's not interesting.<br /> <br /> Also I like how simple you've managed to make the Contracts bit. Whittling the &quot;emotional&quot; Contracts down to a single Contract with multiple facets like the Elemental Contracts is a great idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T09:24:14-07:00","id":551674,"title":"","content":"How tied to the Court specifically does the ritual have to be to be effective? Like, could a small Freehold in LA have a Bruins court and a Trojans court and swap rulers based on who won the last football game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T09:28:28-07:00","id":551676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=551652#post551652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IOne thing I love is that the example Court is such an odd concept. Rather than go with the more by the book stuff like Seasons or Day/Night (which it looks like will be covered in the locations section), the book gives you an idea of just how weird and creative you can get with it. &quot;A town's industries&quot; is <i>not</i> something I would have ever imagined as a Court structure, but dang if it's not interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely second this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T09:52:12-07:00","id":551735,"title":"","content":"I really like this. It does mean there's a bit more logistical work for a given location, but it seems simple enough to work out and I much prefer the &quot;each freehold defines its own story&quot; approach.<br /> <br /> Does the Bulwark just add to Defense, or is there more to it than that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:02:30-07:00","id":551749,"title":"","content":"I'd say that if it ever comes up, the True Fae take a penalty to navigating the Hedge towards a city equal to the mantle of the current reigning party's representative(ie, their Sovereign), but that's a clear houserule that probably won't come up often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:03:04-07:00","id":551751,"title":"","content":"I feel like the Court Creation system is perfect for some of the weirder ideas I've had about Changeling in the past, like:<br /> <br /> Neighbourhood Courts in New York that only cover a handful of city blocks but wield absolute power within them.<br /> <br /> Splintered philosophical Courts in North Chicago, and a strong, unified Court in South Chicago.<br /> <br /> Satirical Courts in Stockholm, where all the Changelings feel the freehold is just a big inside joke.<br /> <br /> Stuff like that. This system is modular and just really effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5408-fetfet","name":"fetfet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5408_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:20:59-07:00","id":551809,"title":"","content":"This is really cool. I love how mechanically light it is, with most of the customization coming in the form of concept. What's the story your freehold tells? What rituals do the courts practice to maintain the bulwark? What emotion does each court represent? What a their Approaches? They're all fairly simple questions that can be thought about from a completely narrative focus, and the framework allows the mechanics to arise naturally from that with very little fuss. This is great because it makes me excited to come up with the Stories for the Freeholds for the major cities in my big crossover project, instead of feeling like more work I have to do.<br /> <br /> I'm intrigued by the idea of Approaches, but not entirely sure what to make of them yet. I think I like them. But I don't fully grok their place in the world yet. Are they supposed to be vulnerabilities or advantages? They seem like a bit of both, which I like, but without knowing how Huntsmen work or what Yearning does, it's not entirely clear why a Huntsman would play into them. I could use more examples of Approaches and how a Huntsman might exploit them (or ignore them, in situations where the drawbacks outweigh the advantages of the Yearning). Also, I'm not clear on how aware the characters are of Approaches.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure why a Freehold needs at least two Courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:24:01-07:00","id":551811,"title":"","content":"On approaches, how I read it is that it's bait, or like creating channels for water. By inviting the Huntsmen to come after you in a particular way, you force them onto your territory, narratively speaking, so you have more control over the outcome by being subversive.<br /> <br /> A freehold needs two courts because it's more interesting that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:46:54-07:00","id":551833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=551811#post551811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On approaches, how I read it is that it's bait, or like creating channels for water. By inviting the Huntsmen to come after you in a particular way, you force them onto your territory, narratively speaking, so you have more control over the outcome by being subversive.<br /> <br /> A freehold needs two courts because it's more interesting that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Related to that - what is Yearning? I have a deep desire to know. So deep, there must be a word for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5408-fetfet","name":"fetfet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5408_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:47:28-07:00","id":551834,"title":"","content":"Hunger, maybe?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, in endeavoring to get people building stuff, would it help if I put up what I have so far on the Paris Courts after I get it lined up with this model?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:52:19-07:00","id":551839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=551811#post551811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On approaches, how I read it is that it's bait, or like creating channels for water. By inviting the Huntsmen to come after you in a particular way, you force them onto your territory, narratively speaking, so you have more control over the outcome by being subversive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's the general idea I got from it as well, but I'm more curious about why the Huntsmen would play into the Changelings' hands like that. I mean, for the Yearning, obviously, but without knowing what Yearning is, I'm intrigued but not totally sold.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=551811#post551811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A freehold needs two courts because it's more interesting that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I usually find more options more interesting than fewer options. It may be more interesting for a Freehold to have multiple Courts more often than not, but it seems like an arbitrary limitation to say they need to have multiple Courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:52:56-07:00","id":551840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=551834#post551834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunger, maybe?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, in endeavoring to get people building stuff, would it help if I put up what I have so far on the Paris Courts after I get it lined up with this model?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more like yearning.<br /> <br /> I'd love to see that. I'll do the same thing with my New York Freehold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5408-fetfet","name":"fetfet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5408_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:53:02-07:00","id":551841,"title":"","content":"One thing I adored about the Seasonal Courts was how well they supported 1e's PTSD metaphor, embodying emotions with heavy ties to how individuals respond to stress. I'm not sure how I feel about loosening up that connection and driving Courts further towards fairytale and further away from what made the original game so well-loved by many survivors that I personally know.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T10:58:35-07:00","id":551848,"title":"","content":"Well, it's not like you lost out on them. The Seasonal Courts are still in there. It's just not as central a feature now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T11:08:51-07:00","id":551856,"title":"","content":"So I was reading and commenting on your mushroom blog the other day talking about how much I love world building. Between Changeling and Werewolf 2e, along with the ability to build Lairs in Beast, I think the OP teams are really hitting the nail on the head with the ability to allow people to customize and create. I could easily see a Changeling group sitting down at the start of a Chronicle, spinning a globe, and throwing a dart at to pick the setting of their next game, then the players and storytellers working together to flesh out the Changeling's history in that location, along with the courts. That can only be a good thing. This also works really, really well with my personal itch to customize and build settings of my own. Well done on making it so flexible and broadly applicable!<br /> <br /> As for cities, here are some thoughts I'm hoping to flesh out when I get time:<br /> <br /> <b>Saskatoon</b> - An ancient &quot;court&quot; based around the Cree Medicine Wheel and the four winds. The North and South cause the seasons to change, while the East and West cause the sun to move across the Sky. There's some debate amongst the Changelings as to weather the Winds were Changelings themselves or True Spirits, but the practice dates back to before the colonial period, and was almost wiped out in the early 1900s. <br /> <br /> <b>Istanbul</b> - There could only be one story that does Istanbul justice, and that is the story of the city itself. Its bulwark is a year long symbolic ritual that reenacts the entirety of cities long history. It begins with the Greek Court, followed by the Rome Court, the Latin Court, the Ottoman Court, and the Ataturk Court, each playing their role before passing it off to the next group of players. <br /> <br /> <b>Abu Dhabi</b> - Abu Dhabi has its history, although its shrouded in the mists of history much more throughly than that of the rest of the Middle East, hence the story that forms their Bulwark is considerably more modern, but even the mortals in the United Arab Emirates could guess it if they had to. Or at least, they could guess part of it. The story could be told in long form and stretch back for generations, but it is really about two brothers, one a staunch traditionalist, the other a genius forward thinker. Shakabut and Zeyad. The last ruler of the Bani Yas tribe before everything changed, and his younger brother, the very architect of that change and the Father of the Nation. Some have suggested that the Al Nayhan family may have been touched by the supernatural, but most are skeptical. The two brothers may not have been changelings, but they were forces of nature unto themselves, and even amongst mortals, the Wyrd must respect their stories. The courts of Abu Dhabi drawn on the city's traditional symbols, The Falcon, The Dhow, The Gazelle (Abu Dhabi means &quot;Father of Gazelles&quot;), The Date Palm, and The Camel. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T11:14:00-07:00","id":551861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=551856#post551856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Istanbul</b> - There could only be one story that does Istanbul justice, and that is the story of the city itself. Its bulwark is a year long symbolic ritual that reenacts the entirety of cities long history. It begins with the Greek Court, followed by the Rome Court, the Latin Court, the Ottoman Court, and the Ataturk Court, each playing their role before passing it off to the next group of players.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I need this. I need this so very bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T11:33:24-07:00","id":551881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=551861#post551861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I need this. I need this so very bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's see if I can't nail down an emotion for each of them then. This is quick and off the top of my head, so I may revise them later. <br /> <br /> <b>Greek</b> - Pride<br /> <br /> <b>Rome</b> - Might<br /> <br /> <b>Latin</b> - Zeal<br /> <br /> <b>Ottoman</b> - Ambition<br /> <br /> <b>Ataturk</b> - Independence<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T11:37:31-07:00","id":551888,"title":"","content":"really dig the new Court system. While I usually like the idea of global groups, the new system makes Changeling feels a lot more of how it is meant to feel, from explaining how the Lost protect them against the Gentry and up to how Courts are meant to be built. As a changeling, whether a story is true or false is less true then telling the story right. The Approach is truly my favorite adjustment- making yourself vulnerable to force your enemies to play the game you want to play? That just sounds awesome. I have to make a Court which its Approach should be a dancing contest :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T11:46:54-07:00","id":551900,"title":"","content":"I enjoyed this, as well as the Toronto writeup. ^_^ I honestly am just really loving the overall shift toward veiling things in terms of narratives and stories. I've always been a big fan of it, and it's done very well in here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=551811#post551811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On approaches, how I read it is that it's bait, or like creating channels for water. By inviting the Huntsmen to come after you in a particular way, you force them onto your territory, narratively speaking, so you have more control over the outcome by being subversive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aye, that was my thinking, too. I'm curious if there are additional rules for Courtless Changelings. It could be that Huntsmen normally get Yearning when causing any sort of unpleasantness to a particular Changeling within a broad spectrum, and Court membership forces a more narrow set of tactics.<br /> <br /> I definitely like the idea that a Changeling in joining a Court commits themselves to something meaningful, and Huntsmen have an easier time getting at them only after disrupting or creating cracks in that commitment. If the larger metaphor is maintaining one's self-determination... perhaps Yearning is the consequence of running into setbacks that undermine one's convictions in living one's life, and makes it easier to leave that real life and slip back into fantasy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A freehold needs two courts because it's more interesting that way. </div> </div> </div>In addition, it seems a big part of the ritual that maintains the Bulwark is transfer of power between Courts -- or at least the chance of such. That's not really a plausible proposition if there's only a single Court.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Added in thoughts on the piece as a whole. 06-12-2015, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T11:51:41-07:00","id":551905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=551848#post551848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it's not like you lost out on them. The Seasonal Courts are still in there. <b>It's just not as central a feature now.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T11:52:45-07:00","id":551907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=551905#post551905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Says you, I'm having a blast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T11:58:36-07:00","id":551914,"title":"","content":"First, I think we need a Grimm Courts of 19th Century Germany for Dark Eras now, with Red Riding Hood, Sleeping Beuty, Cinderella and all others Courts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As to Approches: I like the &quot;con&quot; feel of them, but mechanics do not work with it - I mean in particular Mantle Merit. Approches seems as both blessing and a &quot;curse&quot;, so by this, I would rather put Personal Appoches as 2nd dot of Mantle, and change them with 4th dot. Most Court members should be able to make those, not only most powerfull, with 4 or 5 dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T12:00:20-07:00","id":551916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=551907#post551907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Says you, I'm having a blast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling's main appeal - for me, many of my players, and quite a few others I know - is how the game acts as a metaphor for abuse survivors. Straying away from that is like a Wraith game without depression; I hate to see the lessened focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T12:00:59-07:00","id":551917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=551907#post551907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Says you, I'm having a blast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likewise. If there is any splat that should be localized in its social groups, its changelings. 1e calls out the fact that there aren't enough of them for intercity communication to happen regularly. It seems illogical that the courts would spread so far. Plus, they are fae and stories are supposed to be important to them. It is wonderful that each table can now take time to craft their own city and story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T12:03:44-07:00","id":551921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=551905#post551905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not a good thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are as central as you want them to be. This system puts the choice into the storyteller's hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T12:20:33-07:00","id":551995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=551916#post551916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Changeling's main appeal - for me, many of my players, and quite a few others I know - is how the game acts as a metaphor for abuse survivors. Straying away from that is like a Wraith game without depression; I hate to see the lessened focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Well, it is now broadened out from <i>abuse</i> survivors to <i>trauma </i>survivors, sooooo. Yeah. You know, context.<br /> <br /> 2) The courts are now broadened out to explore more images and ideas to use as metaphors. Creating more room to explore an idea is a good idea.<br /> <br /> Nothing's being strayed from, it's just being expanded. I, for one, enjoy creating local metaphors that make the courts more personal to the changelings in it as an expression of coping and moving on, rather than a unified and more distant expression of the idea.<br /> <br /> And truth be told, I hated the entire &quot;Courts are metaphors for stages of Kubler-Ross model!&quot; argument. It always struck me as shallow. THis isn't a linear game where you hop from court to court. It can be, but it's not inherently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T12:36:53-07:00","id":552009,"title":"","content":"The trauma angle also seems much more emphasized in the Seemings now as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T12:38:55-07:00","id":552016,"title":"","content":"Also, another big thing is that I have not lost the Seasonal Courts. They are still right there, on my shelf(Well, bed right now), their richness and depth forever within my grasp. I have gained freedom and will only lose $30+ for a book that's not even out yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-12-2015, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T12:41:56-07:00","id":552020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=551916#post551916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling's main appeal - for me, many of my players, and quite a few others I know - is how the game acts as a metaphor for abuse survivors. Straying away from that is like a Wraith game without depression; I hate to see the lessened focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>This really doesn't ring true to me, though. What is being lost, exactly? Please help me see that, because right now I just don't. To my understanding of that common reading, the default circumstance of the seasonal Courts suggests that there are four broad responses to abuse. Compared to 2e's more flexible system, allowing for greater variety and nuance, that strikes me as pretty reductive. There are and have always been a multitude of possible ways for survivors to respond and live their lives. All the better that the new system suggests these are often localized, just as different communities can have their own means of coping.<br /> <br /> It may also be that you're not looking at this holistically. Do you also feel the 1e Seemings did a better job of furthering the survivor metaphor than the 2e Seemings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T13:30:32-07:00","id":552100,"title":"","content":"I totally knew it. I knew how Bulwarks were going to work... and I didn't mention it to anyone so I can't boast. Ah well.<br /> <br /> <br /> So on the whole I liked it, a lot. My biggest issue is not in the text, but something I feel is a very important omission from the text. That is explicitly tying it into the core theme of abuse survivors rebuilding their lives.<br /> <br /> The reason I say &quot;explicitly&quot; is that it's kinda there &quot;implicitly&quot;. Snow want to rebuild their ties to mortal society. Hart want to explore their new fae existence. In short, I think these new courts are in the same place as the seasonal courts.<br /> <br /> Every time I pointed out that Spring could be the court that wants new lives in the mortal world; Autumn wants new lives in the fae world; Winter just doesn't want to be hurt again - I had people (including veteran Changeling storytellers) saying it was the single best piece of Changeling advice they've seen.<br /> <br /> And IMO these new courts are in the exact same spot. They are life-aspirations for Changelings trying to rebuild after the durance, but if it isn't made explicit people won't notice just like they didn't notice that about the Seasonal Courts. <hr /><br /> There was one particular area that didn't work for me. This section entitled &quot;Step 3: Ideals and Emotions&quot;. What I didn't like is when it went through the courts and gave them charachter roles like this: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>It is the court of woodsmen, politicians, and professional duelists</i></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I would much prefer it if the game made it clear that a fighter, a woodsman, and occultist, etc could belong to any court but how they'd approach the role is different.<br /> <br /> A copper occultist would be an archaeologist digging up the past, or a necromancer surrounded by the ghosts of the past. A Pine occultist would perform dangerous experiments for knowledge or perform risky rituals with confidence. Hart occultists would brave the hedge or hunt the gentry for their knowledge. A Snow occultist would collaborate with mortals or just study mortal occult practices.<br /> <br /> My suggestion would be to just remove the sentence &quot;it is the court of&quot; from each write up and discuss the concept that Courts don't provide a profession but an approach that could be applied to many somewhere else in the text. <hr /><br /> Something else I would have liked is more mechanical weight on the individual Court rituals. Currently there's the bulwark ritual, which is a Big Deal, and there's Court Rituals that don't have any mechanical effect.<br /> <br /> This is IMO, especially important when the Bulwark ritual falls heavily onto one court. The Iron Freehold's Bulwark ritual is a literal hunt, and what do you know, they have a court based on the hunting industry. I'm completely fine with that, but I would like to see some mechanical weight to the idea that the other courts can't just slack off.<br /> <br /> I could see Courtiers loosing their affinity contracts, emotional harvisting bonus, and/or mantle bonus if the court rituals aren't upheld; but I have a better idea.<br /> <br /> If one Court forgoes it's rituals then there's a crack in the Bulwark:<br /> <br /> Members of the slacking court can be targeted by any Approach in the Freehold. Every other court can be targeted by their own Approach and the slacking Court's Approach. (Personal Approaches still apply). <hr /><br /> One final thing. I wasn't too keen on Mantle providing a Personal Approach. That said if you also got Personal Approaches from Wyrd I wouldn't mind it (I'd still prefer it if it wasn't called &quot;personal&quot; but that's a non-issue)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T13:35:29-07:00","id":552103,"title":"","content":"On Court Rituals, not everything has to have a mechanical effect. Some things should be done, in character, because they're just good things to bring the community together and reinforce their sense of self with and, out of character, because they make for interesting set pieces, whether it really is a block party or it's a setup for something more sinister.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, look at Toronto.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T13:51:59-07:00","id":552112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=552020#post552020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This really doesn't ring true to me, though. What is being lost, exactly? Please help me see that, because right now I just don't. To my understanding of that common reading, the default circumstance of the seasonal Courts suggests that there are four broad responses to abuse. Compared to 2e's more flexible system, allowing for greater variety and nuance, that strikes me as pretty reductive. There are and have always been a multitude of possible ways for survivors to respond and live their lives. All the better that the new system suggests these are often localized, just as different communities can have their own means of coping.<br /> <br /> It may also be that you're not looking at this holistically. Do you also feel the 1e Seemings did a better job of furthering the survivor metaphor than the 2e Seemings?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can only give my take, which is that a broader focus removes the potency of the orignal approach. If you come into the game in 2.ed, the survivor angle will be less prominent. The 4 original courts maps easily to coping mechanisms, while I cannot see that the court of Copper does the same. That was the main draw in 1.ed., that it was a game about overcoming and surviving abuse or tradgedy disgusied as a fairy tale RPG. It seesm that the new edidtion is dillutiong that theme. I mean, at an extreme you could say that it is possible to make a GURPS abusve survivor RPG, but you would have to paint the theme yourself. So I guess you can still play that kind of game with Changeling 2.ed. but it is no longer the central theme in the smae way.. But that is of course just the feeling I get from these spoilers.<br /> <br /> I also felt that the new Seemings have strayed quite a bit. I really thought I would enjoy the new Kith/Seeming interaction, but I findd the implementaiton of the new idea less powerful than I though I would. The original Beast, Ogre and Fairest descriptions were powerhouses of abuse methaphors and farytale logic, these new ones seems tame in comparission. Not to mention too free-flowing, I find that my best characters comes from limitations instead of options, I have hundreds of potential character ideas but need some limits to inspire them. Not a fan of anything goes approaches to character creation.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1228-jhiriit","name":"Jhiriit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T13:57:47-07:00","id":552118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=552103#post552103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Court Rituals, not everything has to have a mechanical effect. Some things should be done, in character, because they're just good things to bring the community together and reinforce their sense of self with and, out of character, because they make for interesting set pieces, whether it really is a block party or it's a setup for something more sinister.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, but I think there's room for both mechanical court rituals and block parties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T14:02:09-07:00","id":552125,"title":"","content":"Maybe in a later book. Keep it simple for the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T14:04:09-07:00","id":552152,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't mind if it was in a later book, but I can't see how it would need more than a couple of paragraphs of text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T14:16:35-07:00","id":552168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jhiriit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=552112#post552112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can only give my take, which is that a broader focus removes the potency of the orignal approach. If you come into the game in 2.ed, the survivor angle will be less prominent. The 4 original courts maps easily to coping mechanisms, while I cannot see that the court of Copper does the same. That was the main draw in 1.ed., that it was a game about overcoming and surviving abuse or tradgedy disgusied as a fairy tale RPG. It seesm that the new edidtion is dillutiong that theme. I mean, at an extreme you could say that it is possible to make a GURPS abusve survivor RPG, but you would have to paint the theme yourself. So I guess you can still play that kind of game with Changeling 2.ed. but it is no longer the central theme in the smae way.. But that is of course just the feeling I get from these spoilers.<br /> <br /> I also felt that the new Seemings have strayed quite a bit. I really thought I would enjoy the new Kith/Seeming interaction, but I findd the implementaiton of the new idea less powerful than I though I would. The original Beast, Ogre and Fairest descriptions were powerhouses of abuse methaphors and farytale logic, these new ones seems tame in comparission. Not to mention too free-flowing, I find that my best characters comes from limitations instead of options, I have hundreds of potential character ideas but need some limits to inspire them. Not a fan of anything goes approaches to character creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking both as someone with PTSD and as someone who knows a <i>lot</i> of other people with it, I feel like the way 2E Seemings are expressed hit much closer to home for me (trust issues, acting out, overdeveloped sense of responsibility, etc) whereas the old Courts/Stages of Grief parallel, while interesting, honestly feels kind of textbook in comparison. The way Courts work now, as TKR mentioned above, seem to be more as a &quot;what now?&quot; kind of thing.<br /> <br /> Note: I'm not saying 2E Seemings are literally stand-ins for &quot;types&quot; of PTSD (whatever that means <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />), simply that the effects of each Seeming (particularly the Clarity mechanics) are very similar to the ways many people cope after going through a traumatic experience. Granted, the Seemings we have yet to see could break this trend, but from the hints we've gotten I strongly doubt it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3738,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","user":"Illuminated Minutia","date":". 06-12-2015, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T14:21:36-07:00","id":552173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=552168#post552168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note: I'm not saying 2E Seemings are literally stand-ins for &quot;types&quot; of PTSD (whatever that means <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />), simply that the effects of each Seeming (particularly the Clarity mechanics) are very similar to the ways many people cope after going through a traumatic experience. Granted, the Seemings we have yet to see could break this trend, but from the hints we've gotten I strongly doubt it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you brought this up. Seemings are more than a function for trauma reaction, they have faerie tale icons at the least to fulfill as well, and more asides.<br /> <br /> Nothing is exactly one-to-one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T15:12:29-07:00","id":552234,"title":"","content":"I have a question concerning monarchs. From my reading of the the court creation doc, it seems that not only does each court get a reigning monarch but the freehold-at-large does as well. Seems like a lot of royalty to me, but perhaps that's by design to create conflict. Does only the freehold monarch gain the benefits of the Crown, then?<br /> <br /> My confusion may stem from &quot;freehold&quot; and &quot;court&quot; being used a bit interchangeably. Aside from this, though, I love this system. It really gives the troupe a way to build up their setting, and in a very different way than the Werewolf pack-building system does. Kudos, Mr. Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T15:18:21-07:00","id":552240,"title":"","content":"If I had the time, I'd really love to try to write-up a Freehold for my hometown of NYC where each court is based on the unique history and culture of each of the 5 boroughs, including such items as the CEO of Manhattan, the Don of Staten Island, and even the King of Queens. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T15:40:10-07:00","id":552279,"title":"","content":"I'd like to try to write up Las Vegas and Los Angeles, myself!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T15:50:25-07:00","id":552286,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to write-up one for Malta for a crossover setting I've been working on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T15:51:03-07:00","id":552287,"title":"","content":"All right, so, what I have so far!<br /> <br /> <b>STEP ONE! THE STORY!</b><br /> <br /> So, as I've mentioned before, I have two stories that form the core of my idea. The first is <a href=\"http://www.pitt.edu/~dash/beauty.html\" target=\"_blank\">Beauty and the Beast</a>, in particular <a href=\"http://www.hulu.com/watch/348225\" target=\"_blank\">Jean Cocteau's version</a> (also check out Kyle Kallgren's <a href=\"http://blip.tv/brows-held-high/brows-held-high-beauty-and-the-beast-part-1-7027567\" target=\"_blank\">amazing review of the piece</a>)-not only because it's a classic faerie tale, and a classic French faerie tale at that, but because of it's surrealism and many, <i>many</i> parallels towards Changeling's own symbolism. Also because it's awesome. Mainly because it's awesome.<br /> <br /> The second one is my favorite faerie tale, <a href=\"http://www.pitt.edu/~dash/perrault02.html\" target=\"_blank\">Little Red Riding Hood by Perrault</a>, and the story it gets it's roots from, <a href=\"http://www.sjsu.edu/faculty/harris/StudentProjects/Student_FairyTales/WebProject/Fairy%20Tales/The%20Story%20of%20Grandmother.htm\" target=\"_blank\">The Grandmother's Tale</a>. I would be remiss, though, if I also didn't admit that I'm drawing a lot on my personal favorite incarnation of the tale, that being <a href=\"http://tale-of-tales.com/ThePath/\" target=\"_blank\">The Path</a>-seriously, explore the website and it's many tidbits of information, then go buy this game and get emotionally traumatized by it, it's amazing. Not only is there surrealism, but all the incarnations have a lot to do with adolescence(as a concept-I'm 26 and I hope am an adolescent in the way I use that word), which is one of my favorite things to play around with in stories, and it neatly captures cynicism that is missing from Beauty and the Beast.<br /> <br /> While I'm not going full tilt with it as a story, I'd also be lying if I said it wasn't in here, so I must mention that I'm also drawing a lot from <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6TQFlVcPyUA\" target=\"_blank\">Revolutionary Girl Utena</a>, which is also amazing* and why haven't you watched it yet. Like seriously, if I tried to leave it out, it would sneak in anyways. It's my favorite anime. Now it does carry a similar motif triad of the Maiden, Wild One, and Woodsman in the form of Princess, Witch, and Prince(albeit, with more stuffed in there), and that dynamic plays out a lot, but I wanted to include something like the Dueling system, particularly as it's executed in the Third Arc(based on the Nozomi releases), because I wanted to include some of that swashbuckler feel from the Dark Era to color both the romance and cynicism of the setting, and also because the dueling for the role of the Engaged and the utilization of 'brides' were motifs I wanted to use to bring in intimacy with the setting and as a concept. The words'll probably be different, though the grand roles of the Freehold for the Bulwark might be referenced as the Engaged still. I also want to find a way to incorporate the Rose Gate into the setting of the Bulwark. But mostly, I liked the idea of Dueling as a mechanic that is a regular enough thing in the Courts, something that's important for the society.<br /> <br /> So, the basics of the story, the common points: You have the Maiden(Hood/Belle/Princess), an icon of innocence(and several more concepts), wandering into the woods(Hedge/World) to benefit another(the Grandmother/the Father/\u2026Wakaba? Is there a fourth archetype here, easily forgotten?) and ends up in the clutches of the Wild One(The Wolf/The Beast/The Witch), who brings the Maiden into greater knowledge with the risk of ruin.* A Woodsman(\u2026.The Woodsman/Avenant aka Gaston/The Prince) comes along in time and, seeing the Maiden in danger of the Wild One, attempts to kill the captor. The particulars of the story and its conclusions varies throughout history, and creates a feature of the Bulwark.<br /> <br /> *Yes, I know the Beast from Cocteau\u2019s version is actually already kind and just has to be loved, essentially, but the icon on an older level has to do with either being consumed by the avatar of the world/subconscious self or taming the avatar.<br /> <br /> <b>STEP TWO! THE BULWARK!</b><br /> <br /> So, the Freehold finds people to fill in the three central roles of the Maiden, Wild One, and Woodsman, collectively called the Engaged(complete with all double entendres), possibly as a result of duels related to the role, probably to refine the character of each role. The Wild One, in particular, should be risky \u2018character\u2019-I don\u2019t want to absolutely say it\u2019s a role reserved for enemies and traitors, but the person in the role must be openly dangerous or disruptive. I imagine the other roles try to generate people who most fit the role too, but the Wild One is the most important one to nail. The Engaged have a period of time where they\u2026engage one another, redeeming or seducing one another away fulfillments. The sum point and fulfillment of the Bulwark comes, on the appointed day, when the three gather around the Rose Gate and \u2018kill\u2019 one of them by shoving them. The base idea is that if the Wild One is \u2018tamed\u2019, the Woodsman is considered to be a murderous representation of the Huntsmen and thrown out, and if the Wild One \u2018consumes\u2019 the Maiden, then the Wild One is the representation of the True Fae and the goblin worlds and must be slain, though various interpretations have since happened, in particular the Death of the Maiden and the various interpretation that support that. So long as two unite to defy the third and throw them beyond the Gate, everything works. It\u2019s romantic for two, it\u2019s cynical for one, it asks some hard questions about roles and outsiders and all that stuff.<br /> <br /> Thiiiiiiiis is up in the air, though. When I first had the idea, it really was \u201cIf the Wild One can be \u2018redeemed\u2019, then the Huntsman dies, if the Wild One is more like the Wolf, than he dies\u201d, this sort of binary conclusion. The Maiden is a \u2018judge\u2019 of sorts, with the Wild One and the Woodsman as \u2018executioners\u2019 at the Maiden\u2019s call. I\u2019m not wholly sure if I like this form though, and I have no idea what happens after someone is consigned beyond the Rose Gate(allegorical death, obviously, but in regards to Utena, no one actually dies, and instead claims the ire of the Millions Swords of Hate. Possibly banishment for the next cycle). I imagine they can come back, but there is a risk with that thought.<br /> <br /> One thing I like about this setup, though, is that on top of the basic reward from the Bulwark, a \u2018Fate\u2019 can play out as a result of the remaining Engaged, kind of a small bonus for the turn out(I have no idea what sort of rewards). This runs the risk of making the ritual \u2018political\u2019 rather than \u2018spiritual\u2019, which risks ruining the Bulwark, although again I don\u2019t know exactly what does what. The story demands sincerity, but the Sovereigns demand resources.<br /> <br /> <b>STEP THREE! IDEALS AND EMOTIONS!</b><br /> <br /> Here I only have a motif and an idea. I\u2019m endeared to the idea of calling them the Rose Courts of Paris, with each court being a colored rose(yes, that reeks of the war of roses, so I\u2019m not sold on it). I want three or five(not four), with the first three being the White Rose, the Red Rose, and the Black Rose, followed by the Blue Rose and the Yellow/Gold Rose. Each court should revolve around ideas of what the signature roles should be like-What defines the Maiden, what defines the Wild One, and what defines the Woodsman, and has a romantic ideal and a cynical outlook. And finally, each should have something exterior to that. Oh yeah, and a summary emotion.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t have anything for that.<br /> <br /> <b>STEP FOUR! DESIGN THE COURTS!</b><br /> <br /> Aaaaand nothing here. I haven\u2019t had a lot of time to really dig after I got this far thanks to school. Dueling should come back in here.<br /> <br /> So, that\u2019s where I got!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-12-2015, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T16:20:44-07:00","id":552324,"title":"","content":"Arc, I had some ideas, but of a slightly different line. In this, the chosen Hope and the Despair (Maiden and Wild One, in your terms) engage in a chase across the snow-shrouded streets of a city at midnight, with it ending if the Hope evades the Despair for an hour, or the Despair catches the Hope. In either case, the Judgement (the Woodsman), a member of a local Entitlement, comes in, and draws a sacrifice from the loser. The sacrifice must be something important, and it must be sealed in blood. The Winner then is crowned the monarch for the year. So the loser represents, retroactively, the old year, a painful (literally) reminder of what has been lost and the scars that bind the Lost together, and their sacrifice of aprt of their life keeps the True Fae at bay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T16:27:08-07:00","id":552328,"title":"","content":"Goblin Vows are now Court Merits? Great! I wonder how they work in the new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T16:33:51-07:00","id":552333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=552324#post552324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arc, I had some ideas, but of a slightly different line. In this, the chosen Hope and the Despair (Maiden and Wild One, in your terms) engage in a chase across the snow-shrouded streets of a city at midnight, with it ending if the Hope evades the Despair for an hour, or the Despair catches the Hope. In either case, the Judgement (the Woodsman), a member of a local Entitlement, comes in, and draws a sacrifice from the loser. The sacrifice must be something important, and it must be sealed in blood. The Winner then is crowned the monarch for the year. So the loser represents, retroactively, the old year, a painful (literally) reminder of what has been lost and the scars that bind the Lost together, and their sacrifice of aprt of their life keeps the True Fae at bay.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh. Hmm. Ideas.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, going more in line what I had for the beginning, the loser becomes the fourth archetype? Hmm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-12-2015, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T16:59:42-07:00","id":552352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=551916#post551916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Changeling's main appeal - for me, many of my players, and quite a few others I know - is how the game acts as a metaphor for abuse survivors. Straying away from that is like a Wraith game without depression; I hate to see the lessened focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am an abuse survivor. Numerous members of my team are abuse survivors. We literally made this choice because abuse is such a unique and personal thing, we felt that trying to encapsulate all our experiences into one paradigm just didn't work, and diminished the potential value of the metaphor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T17:01:39-07:00","id":552357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=552100#post552100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I totally knew it. I knew how Bulwarks were going to work... and I didn't mention it to anyone so I can't boast. Ah well.<br /> <br /> <br /> So on the whole I liked it, a lot. My biggest issue is not in the text, but something I feel is a very important omission from the text. That is explicitly tying it into the core theme of abuse survivors rebuilding their lives.<br /> <br /> The reason I say &quot;explicitly&quot; is that it's kinda there &quot;implicitly&quot;. Snow want to rebuild their ties to mortal society. Hart want to explore their new fae existence. In short, I think these new courts are in the same place as the seasonal courts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm really glad this came across implicitly. That was totally the intention, and I think Marianne (our Courts writer) rocked it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T18:13:34-07:00","id":552397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=552333#post552333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh. Hmm. Ideas.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, going more in line what I had for the beginning, the loser becomes the fourth archetype? Hmm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps the loser is called something like &quot;the outcast&quot;, taking a role that falls outside of the normal court structure, and has a place in the Freehold as something akin to a priest ijn a confessional? That means choosing each person to be Hope and Despair is very important, as you have to consider how they will behave should they lose as well as if they should win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T18:36:35-07:00","id":552439,"title":"","content":"I must admit, this is very awesome! Will we be seeing more about the Iron Hold?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm eager to begin work. I already have three freeholds waiting for some flesh; now it's time to start getting to work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T18:36:35-07:00","id":552440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=552397#post552397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps the loser is called something like &quot;the outcast&quot;, taking a role that falls outside of the normal court structure, and has a place in the Freehold as something akin to a priest ijn a confessional? That means choosing each person to be Hope and Despair is very important, as you have to consider how they will behave should they lose as well as if they should win.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking about that. The Forest is a prominent icon in the three stories I referenced, and at the start of the story, there's always someone who incites the Maiden(I need better role names) to enter it. The Grandmother needs bread and other such things delivered by Little Red Riding Hood. The Father plucks a rose, earns the Beast's Ire, and only earns his freedom by promising Belle's return. Utena...well, Utena is Prince and Princess in the beginning, or Woodsman and Maiden in our case, but regardless, if Wakaba hadn't done her schtick with the letter, Utena would never have ended up challenging Saionji and entering the Forest, and thus enter the Duels. On top of that, it creates three roles related to the Forest(greater metaphor at work her than just The Hedge) and thus a sense of three points of adolescence, and a <i>second</i> power trinity. It also feels like something can be used as a dynamic for freehold functional structure, tying the sense of the personal interior world to the wider world. I'm not sure I'd call it the Outcast though. Grandma has too fucked up a house to make it that easy.<br /> <br /> Unrelated to that, part of the reason I like the idea of the Rose Courts is prominence of roses as a metaphorical motif in these stories. Even Little Red Riding Hood ends up having incarnations that use it as a minor underline of the more overt iconography. think I might make the first three Red, Blue,and Yellow though. I dunno.<br /> <br /> Unrelated to either of those, I really need emotions that serve as a lens on this entire affair. I don't think I can avoid love (though I might be able to stretch it out). I'm juggling Hope and Despair.<br /> <br /> Unrelated to those three-well, no, <i>somewhat related to the first part</i>, there's some kind of obvious parallel between the Grandma's House and the Dueling Area/Rose Gate on a larger idea front. Does the BEast's treasure hold, or even the castle, tie into those two as well? Maybe if we hack it up some.<br /> <br /> Semi-related to the last point, part of the appeal to the stories is that they are analogous to the lives of changelings. The manipulation of the frame is probably cathartic for changelings, it's just a matter of how it goes and why it does that makes up the courts.<br /> <br /> I imagine the court rulers of the two Engaged who succeed run the Freehold. The Sovereigns run a real risk of screwing things up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-12-2015, 10:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T19:07:25-07:00","id":552473,"title":"","content":"On an unrelated note, I'm <i>really</i> curious about Huntsmen now. Like I get that they're basically Nazgul to the Gentry's Sauron, but with how well all these other changes have been meshing in to the game's core metaphors, I have to wonder how exactly the Huntsmen will fit in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T19:12:18-07:00","id":552477,"title":"","content":"Dave knows what he's doing. I imagine they'll have a foil quality to them like most other antagonists in Changeling.<br /> <br /> EDIT: According the latest post thing, I am now Zeal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T20:01:46-07:00","id":552494,"title":"","content":"I assume Yearning is a sort of pseudo Power Stat, or a pool that the Huntsman spends to activate the really nasty powers (retrieving an Icon and using it to track their quarry, asking a favor from their patron Fae, and gaining the legal right to attempt recapture).<br /> <br /> Given its name, I also suspect we may have a hint to what motivates them; they desperately all want something the Gentry have, and the Gentry will pay them it if they get new slaves.<br /> <br /> (Also fits in with the very human BBEG of my current project, actually-he Yearns for eternal youth and ever-greater power, especially wealth. So the Adept of Bleak Omens offered it, in return for being a new &quot;wild card&quot; capable of ignoring a Bulwark..).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T20:19:11-07:00","id":552506,"title":"","content":"David...<br /> <br /> I just noticed that Santa Claus and his yearly trip to deliver toys is a <u><i><b>perfect</b></i></u> Bulwark. Please tell me I'm just seeing things.<br /> <br /> Man, what Approaches would the Huntsmen use to try and drag Kris Kringle off to Arcardia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T20:28:47-07:00","id":552511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=552506#post552506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">David...<br /> <br /> I just noticed that Santa Claus and his yearly trip to deliver toys is a <u><i><b>perfect</b></i></u> Bulwark. Please tell me I'm just seeing things.<br /> <br /> Man, what Approaches would the Huntsmen use to try and drag Kris Kringle off to Arcardia?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZgP0aUKlmNw\" data-code=\"ZgP0aUKlmNw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ZgP0aUKlmNw/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Not hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T20:39:47-07:00","id":552513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=552473#post552473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On an unrelated note, I'm <i>really</i> curious about Huntsmen now. Like I get that they're basically Nazgul to the Gentry's Sauron, but with how well all these other changes have been meshing in to the game's core metaphors, I have to wonder how exactly the Huntsmen will fit in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ditto. I can see at least one possible angle. The Huntsmen drag Changelings back to Arcadia -- take them back to the world of fantasy where they were wholly without agency and self-determination. From the Courts teaser, Approaches are how a Huntsman can work against a target Changeling Courtier, and thus the most likely angle getting them back to Arcadia. Something all the Approaches have in common is that they attack or subvert or twist the strengths and ideals that the Court represents to the Changeling. The Silver Court tries to beat the Huntsmen at their own game? Show them how much they aren't even players. The Brass Court embraces faith? Make that faith lead them astray. A Copper Courtier takes pride in her handiwork? Use that handiwork to destroy all pride she feels in it.<br /> <br /> A Seeming is the means by which a Changeling takes back her life. I feel a Court is a philosophical compass a Changeling adopts for direction in living her life once she has it back. A Huntsman undermines the hell out of the direction and ideals she chose. It can make her doubt in them and doubt in herself, make her wonder if she really can live her life or even if she's actually in control. That kind of doubt makes it harder to fight the forces dragging her out of the real world and life she fought so hard to claim and to build. I feel the Huntsman may fit in as the sorts of tribulations and setbacks and injustices that can somtimes make it hard to even bother <i>trying</i> to exercise one's agency.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=552477#post552477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: According the latest post thing, I am now Zeal.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a fun game these forums play, every once in a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T21:13:33-07:00","id":552524,"title":"","content":"I would like to get a gander at Contracts, now that this is up. See how Changeling powers actually work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T21:14:12-07:00","id":552526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=552352#post552352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am an abuse survivor. Numerous members of my team are abuse survivors. We literally made this choice because abuse is such a unique and personal thing, we felt that trying to encapsulate all our experiences into one paradigm just didn't work, and diminished the potential value of the metaphor.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know that's a really good point. I'd previously been torn between the new system making better fae and the old system making a better metaphor; not I'm just firmly in favour of the new system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=552357#post552357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm really glad this came across implicitly. That was totally the intention, and I think Marianne (our Courts writer) rocked it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be careful about using me as a yardstick; like I said I saw the same implicit meaning in the Seasonal Courts but even veteren Changeling Storytellers told me it was new information to them when I brought it up.<br /> <br /> Actually, if you don't mind me asking. You said it's intentionally implicit not explicit. What made you choose to do it that way? It's so different to my natural inclinations, I have to ask. I might even learn something from the answer.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T21:53:31-07:00","id":552543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=552526#post552526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually, if you don't mind me asking. You said it's intentionally implicit not explicit. What made you choose to do it that way? It's so different to my natural inclinations, I have to ask. I might even learn something from the answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, the more explicit you make a metaphor, the more holes people are going to find in it.<br /> <br /> That's fine if your metaphor is like, &quot;These were-elephants are a metaphor for Wall Street fat cats.&quot; That's something pretty much everyone gets, and there's not really a lot of nuance to the issue. Even if someone disagrees with the metaphor, it pretty much goes as far as &quot;I disagree with this metaphor.&quot; <br /> <br /> But if the metaphor is for the experience of dealing with abuse, that's a much more nuanced issue. It's very personal. It's unique from case-to-case. While we have textbook approaches to these things, even your 101 level textbooks tell you &quot;this isn't the same for everyone; these rules don't apply in every case.&quot; So if you make your metaphor explicit, with hard statements, you run the risk of making someone feel as if you've invalidated your experience, that their experience is &quot;not the real way this happens&quot;. That hurts, because you're essentially alienating someone that's been hardcore alienated. <br /> <br /> Also, it lets you choose your level of involvement. Explicit metaphor beats you over the head. It puts a huge neon sign over the door that says, &quot;HERE THERE BE MONSTERS.&quot; And even if someone's generally cool with the idea of dealing with abuse in a game, maybe they want to divest themselves from it a little. Explicit metaphors don't really let you do that. Implicit metaphors hold your hand through that, but you can take your hand back whenever you want. It can just be a Court; you can walk it back a bit without needing to step away from the game entirely. <br /> <br /> I hope that makes sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T23:33:31-07:00","id":552594,"title":"","content":"The reason Courts must create an Opening for the <br /> Huntman... Is the same one the Gentry cannot make themselves totally invincible in their own realms or deny a changeling contester a (very) small chance to win ? That the Wyrd doesn't like that way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T23:41:33-07:00","id":552596,"title":"","content":"That makes perfect sense <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I can follow your logic and I agree with it. The only difference between you an me on this is that we're coming at it from different starting points.<br /> <br /> You came at this from the perspective that Changelings were a metaphor for real life abuse survivors. I wasn't thinking of it as a metaphor at all. I mean sure, I agree that changelings are a metaphor for real life abuse survivors, but in setting most changelings are completely literal abuse survivors who suffered at the hands of the True Fae and survived. I was approaching the Courts from an in setting literal perspective.<br /> <br /> So the Court of Snow might be a metaphor for an abuse survivor learning to trust again and rebuild a socail life. But it's also literally the Court that says to freshly escaped Changelings &quot;The changes are superficial, you're still human, if you want to reestablish yourself in human society join us and we'll help you&quot;.<br /> <br /> So in conclusion. I agree that Court-as-metaphor should be subtle. But I felt that the idea that Changelings choose a Court based on what kind of new life they wish to build is a literal in character phenomenon. And literal in charachter phenomina don't need to be subtlety implied. So I feel the Courts write up would be improved by a short paragraph that says something like &quot;A Court's Ideal describes the kind of life it's members aspire to build. Most Changelings choose a court based on it's Ideal alone. A changeling's affinity for the courts emotion, typical aptitudes, and other aspects will be reflected in Mantle and Goodwill but it is the Court's Ideal that attracts new members&quot;.<br /> <br /> The metaphorical connections between Courts / ideals and real life abuse survivors, both in general and in specific courts, can and should remain subtle and implicit <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T01:14:14-07:00","id":552690,"title":"","content":"In one of the previous thread, I made a big mess out of how much I didn't like the change that was done to my beloved changeling (the fairest). This might have come across as me being &quot;conservative&quot; and wanting to stick to the ways I am used to.<br /> <br /> Not here. Oh my God is this so much cooler than what the original changeling has given to us. This is exactly what I meant when I said that I wanted the game to give you thousands of options, thousands of doors to open and explore, to give the players and the storytellers a great option for creating exactly what they think will be cool in their campaign.<br /> I also love that the specific court-effects are more powerful and thematic compared to old changeling (spring can buy contacts cheaper, wee?).<br /> <br /> Since this is just a draft I shall not complain about the writing as much as try and make it more clear when you are talking about the Freehold monarch versus the Court monarch. For instance, does all court monarchs get the &quot;Crown&quot;-effect or is that only the Freehold monarch? Does the Freehold monarch get a specific (mechanical) bonus that the other monarchs don't get?<br /> <br /> Keep up the great work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T08:56:49-07:00","id":553114,"title":"","content":"Talking this over with my wife, she was uncomfortable with the use of stories in the Freehold because it seemed like the changelings were being forced to play by the rules of their captors, like they didn't escape. I argued that it was, in fact, the opposite. While captives, they were forced to adhere to their captor's story. Now that they have escaped, they have defined their own story and, if their captor wants to engage them, they have to do it on <b>their</b> terms. It is like they are turning the city into a faerie realm where they are in charge and have the home ground advantage and the rules are in their favor. She is unconvinced. Interested to hear other people's thoughts on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T11:13:36-07:00","id":553256,"title":"","content":"I like this. Opens up a lot of opportunity for creative ideas and philosophies--while being simple enough if formula as not to scare off newcomers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T11:41:05-07:00","id":553271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=553114#post553114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talking this over with my wife, she was uncomfortable with the use of stories in the Freehold because it seemed like the changelings were being forced to play by the rules of their captors, like they didn't escape. I argued that it was, in fact, the opposite. While captives, they were forced to adhere to their captor's story. Now that they have escaped, they have defined their own story and, if their captor wants to engage them, they have to do it on <b>their</b> terms. It is like they are turning the city into a faerie realm where they are in charge and have the home ground advantage and the rules are in their favor. She is unconvinced. Interested to hear other people's thoughts on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the answer to this one is complex.<br /> <br /> Compared to 1E your wife is right. They still live by faerie rules and they have to otherwise they'll be recaptured. The Keeper looms large saying &quot;be fae or be mine&quot;. Changelings simply can't put them behind him; while in IE you could quite easily have a game where the risk of being recaptured basically doesn't come up; and it I think the books even said that most Changelings wont' even face at attempt at recapture.<br /> <br /> On other other hand you're correct that Changelings are defining the story and setting the rules. Their freedom is in danger, but they have freedom to be endangered.<br /> <br /> I kinda prefered 1E here. Though I do like the new Bulkwark mechanics. A combination of both would be my preference 19 out of 20 Changelings will never have their freedom attacked; but all of them think they're number 20 and so work hard to keep safe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T11:45:19-07:00","id":553310,"title":"","content":"There's an arc implied here, it's worth noting- Forced to play to Stranger's rules, you then make a choice to play by the Freehold's rules, then you eventually develop your own rules that people have to play by(Personal Approaches), and finally transcending beyond the need for a story with the conquest of your Stranger in his world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T12:09:17-07:00","id":553321,"title":"","content":"I would want to return to mine points, if someone could help here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=551914#post551914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, I think we need a Grimm Courts of 19th Century Germany for Dark Eras now, with Red Riding Hood, Sleeping Beauty, Cinderella and all others Courts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As to Approches: I like the &quot;con&quot; feel of them, but mechanics do not work with it - I mean in particular Mantle Merit. Approches seems as both blessing and a &quot;curse&quot;, so by this, I would rather put Personal Appoches as 2nd dot of Mantle, and change them with 4th dot. Most Court members should be able to make those, not only most powerfull, with 4 or 5 dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T13:42:24-07:00","id":553371,"title":"","content":"Okay.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=551914#post551914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to Approches: I like the &quot;con&quot; feel of them, but <b>mechanics do not work with it</b> - I mean in particular Mantle Merit. Approches seems as both blessing and a &quot;curse&quot;, so by this, I would rather put Personal Appoches as 2nd dot of Mantle, and change them with 4th dot. Most Court members should be able to make those, not only most powerfull, with 4 or 5 dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a problem with the statement I've put in bold. We can't make judgments about whether the mechanics work until we actually <i>have</i> all the mechanics. We have no idea what Yearning does, how the Huntsmen operate against Courtless Changelings,* or how the Huntsmen mechanics work in general. All of those things are needed to establish the context in which Approaches matter, so we can't determine if the Approach mechanics work until we do. It's kinda bad form to just assume they don't, sight unseen.<br /> <br /> * Though the text implies pretty strongly that they'll be coming in whatever way they please. And that means the Huntsman in question gets to play to <i>its own</i> strengths, rather than the strengths the Changeling has taken for herself.<br /> <br /> As for swapping 2nd and 4th, it's possible this could just be a matter of taste. Again, I don't think we have the wherewithal to say yet. We don't know how valuable and useful 2e Goblin Vows are, for instance. Thematically, I kinda see it working better as-is. An Approach is called &quot;the Court's greatest strength,&quot; narrowing the direction of attack that a Huntsmen can take. Remember that a Personal Approach isn't just one specific to the Changeling, but specific to how the Changeling &quot;[fulfills] the ideals and story of the court.&quot; It makes perfect sense to me that a refinement of the Court's greatest strength is only open to those who have established an especially deep mystic connection to and embodied the ideals of the Court, as represented by a higher Mantle.<br /> <br /> I mean, depending on how Goblin Vows work and the context around Approaches, it's unlikely to break anything if you want to shuffle around the order as a houserule. I just don't see an issue with the default setup, given what we know so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T19:15:57-07:00","id":553640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=553114#post553114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talking this over with my wife, she was uncomfortable with the use of stories in the Freehold because it seemed like the changelings were being forced to play by the rules of their captors, like they didn't escape. I argued that it was, in fact, the opposite. While captives, they were forced to adhere to their captor's story. Now that they have escaped, they have defined their own story and, if their captor wants to engage them, they have to do it on <b>their</b> terms. It is like they are turning the city into a faerie realm where they are in charge and have the home ground advantage and the rules are in their favor. She is unconvinced. Interested to hear other people's thoughts on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your wife is WRONG, <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> just kidding. There isn't enough context to understand the Freehold situation in general, but I would liken it more to the rules of society. An abuse victim can't grab a baseball bat, find their abuser after 5 years, and bash the bastard's brains out. The rules are at a higher level than victim and abuser. Telling stories are probably the rules that govern changelings and gentry. Changelings make a story that resonates with them and gives them strength.<br /> <br /> Also like to point out when I checked out Courts the day it was released it was crowded, so there must be lots of people interested. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:20:16-07:00","id":553689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=553114#post553114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talking this over with my wife, she was uncomfortable with the use of stories in the Freehold because it seemed like the changelings were being forced to play by the rules of their captors, like they didn't escape. I argued that it was, in fact, the opposite. While captives, they were forced to adhere to their captor's story. Now that they have escaped, they have defined their own story and, if their captor wants to engage them, they have to do it on <b>their</b> terms. It is like they are turning the city into a faerie realm where they are in charge and have the home ground advantage and the rules are in their favor. She is unconvinced. Interested to hear other people's thoughts on this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. That's exactly it. You took control. Now, if they want to fuck with you, they have to do it YOUR way. You get home turf advantage, because you decided on a home turf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T20:59:05-07:00","id":553764,"title":"","content":"Minor question for the thread: should I move the my Paris experiment to another thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:11:20-07:00","id":553797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=553764#post553764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minor question for the thread: should I move the my Paris experiment to another thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>I say leave it here. David said he wanted feedback on the process, and that lets you comment on it as you make Paris. I plan on doing something similar for the Courts of Abu Dhabi and Istanbul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:25:27-07:00","id":553830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=553797#post553797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I say leave it here. David said he wanted feedback on the process, and that lets you comment on it as you make Paris. I plan on doing something similar for the Courts of Abu Dhabi and Istanbul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Leave it here. We're cool. Unless you particularly want to delineate it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T21:43:57-07:00","id":553856,"title":"","content":"Yes please; that way, it'll be easier to find later.<br /> <br /> On a different topic: the current Mantle set-up is so simple, I have a small desire to hack it for other stuff. The big one being as an add-on for Mystery Cult Initiation, but I dunno if I'll end up sharing that (it'll probably go scrap heap, to be honest.)<br /> <br /> However... the Freehold of the Ring would be... interesting. I actually have the Tale (Lord of the Rings, natch) and a couple of ideas for Bulwarks (ranging from symbolically reenacting the Ride of Rohan or the Battle for the Shire, to straight-up reenacting <i>the entire plot</i> in symbolic terms. And your Motley has been chosen as the Fellowship, of course).<br /> <br /> I don't have ideas for how the Courts would be divided yet, though, so... kinda stuck there. If I felt really sassy, I'd pull the focus back a bit and have the Courts represent different portrayals of Middle Earth (the Silmarillion, the Lord of the Rings, and the Hobbit, of course; I can kinda see how it would fit together... somehow)<i>.</i><br /> <br /> Other ideas:<br /> <br /> <b>The Hairy Freehold</b> - the Tale is <a href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=SP3eegpgalIC&amp;pg=PA25&amp;lpg=PA25&amp;dq=big+hairy+man+gonna+git+you&amp;source=bl&amp;ots=jVt9qtUJY9&amp;sig=5Or2hYLddHzdbOlws9FzEKHGhAQ&amp;hl=en&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=0CB8Q6AEwAGoVChMIxeP01qqOxgIVh3ySCh0SdwBq#v=onepage&amp;q&amp;f=false\" target=\"_blank\">Wiley and the Hairy Man</a>. The Bulwark is <i>deceptively</i> simple, with the principle players being Wiley and the Hairy Man (a stand-in for the True Fae). Over the course of the year, the Hairy Man must actively try to capture Wiley; however, if Wiley can fool him three times, the Hairy One must relent and they (and the Gentry) must leave the Freehold alone until the ritual fails.<br /> <br /> Why is it deceptively simple? Because the Hairy Man isn't really necessary - he's just the least dangerous of all the options. After all, a Huntsman (or the real deal) <i>will</i> do the trick as well... but only for that one. And only for so long.<br /> <br /> I think the Courts would be based around interpretations of what, exactly, counts as &quot;fooling&quot; the Hairy Man. Maybe. It could be interesting.<br /> <br /> <b>The Labrynthine Court</b>... <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dDkp7GysvbY\" target=\"_blank\">do I need to say anything?</a> The <i>entire</i> plot of that movie would be a <i>perfect</i> Bulwark.<br /> <br /> On that note, the <b>Freehold of Bowie</b> would be <i>amazing</i>. I mean... come on. Make up something coherent that combines the Diamond Dogs, Ziggie Stardust, The Man Who Sold The World, and Space Oddity... it would be so beautiful. I think I would need to listen to those albums again before doing anything like that.<br /> <br /> Or the <b>Nameless Court</b>. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8JIQJc8WU7U\" target=\"_blank\">Quadrophenia</a> makes an excellent Tale... I just need to figure out how to tease the rest out of it. Yeah, Gentry, try getting through <i>the awakening of a disaffected youth into full dissatisfaction with society</i>!<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> No. The. Best. Freehold:<br /> <br /> <b>The Tollbooth Freehold</b><br /> <i>The Tale:</i> The Phantom Tollbooth.<br /> <i>The Bulwark:</i> A traveller (let us call him Milo) must travel to rescue beautiful Rhyme and sweet Reason from within the Hedge, and in doing so must rekindle his sense of wonder at the beauty of experience and thought.<br /> <i>The Courts</i>: The Court of Letters and the Court of Numbers, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T01:11:32-07:00","id":554032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=553856#post553856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that note, the <b>Freehold of Bowie</b> would be <i>amazing</i>. I mean... come on. Make up something coherent that combines the Diamond Dogs, Ziggie Stardust, The Man Who Sold The World, and Space Oddity... it would be so beautiful. I think I would need to listen to those albums again before doing anything like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty far out, man... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I've been brainstorming ideas for a San Francisco Freehold; it's been observed before that the Bay Area seems well suited to being a setting for Changeling, and I live in nearby Santa Cruz, so I have a fair amount of familiarity with the area. Here's my basic idea; more to come soon, hopefully:<br /> <br /> <b>The Freehold of Gold Mountain</b><br /> <br /> San Francisco's freehold emerged in the waning years of the California Gold Rush, when the heady days of the 49'ers were already starting to fade into legend and the new city was settling into a modicum of stability. The first Changelings to emerge from the Hedge into the Bay Area were mostly recent arrivals who had been drawn to California by the promise of wealth and a better life, particularly poor Chinese immigrants whose relative invisibility made them easy prey for the Others. The name &quot;Gold Mountain&quot; is itself borrowed from the Cantonese <i>Gam Saan </i>(\u91d1\u5c71), and Chinese folklore has had a major impact on the structure and rituals of the freehold.<br /> <br /> Gold is the central metaphor around which the courts of Gold Mountain orient themselves, representing a whole host of physical and philosophical treasures which Changelings of the freehold seek. The highest law of the land is the Golden Rule, which states that &quot;he who has the gold, makes the rules.&quot; The Changelings of San Francisco hold periodic elections, during which each court nominates one of their own to be the leader of the Freehold as a whole. Candidates gain the support of rival courts by buying it; each makes an offer of some sort to those who would endorse them as ruler, and whoever makes the best offer is ushered into power - after they pay up, of course.<br /> <br /> Four courts vie jockey for power in the Freehold (though I haven't quite come up with names for them), each of which grounds its philosophy in a unifying narrative:<br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Greed</b> claims to be the oldest of the courts, and this may well be true. They tell the story of the Gold Rush itself, when brave men risked all in the pursuit of unimaginable wealth, and the most capable among them seized it and built legacies of power and prestige. Unapologetic capitalists and masters of the strange economy of the Fey, the court does not see greed as a sin, but rather a fundamental part of human nature that motivates people to compete and achieve, and in doing so build a better world.<br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Fellowship</b> tells the story of the Golden Nugget, in which a pair of true friends and hard workers refuse to bicker over a treasure that cannot be shared, and in the end are rewarded twofold. They stress the importance of pulling ones own weight, but also of helping out one's fellow Changeling, so that the community as a whole may know strength and prosperity.<br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Anger</b> tells the story of an outlaw, Joaquin Murietta, who is said to have lost his brother and wife to a drunken mob. After ruthlessly hunting down the men responsible and exacting his revenge, he took to robbing Anglo miners of their gold and distributing it to poor Mexicans struggling under the yoke of an unjust society. While many in the other courts challenge accuracy of this tale, the Court of Anger cares less about the historical Murietta than it does about his role as an archetype of righteous anger and and rebellion. They seek to embolden the poor and the powerless and stoke anger and resentment against the injustice of the status quo, and aren't above using violence and robbery as tools in pursuit of their goals.<br /> <br /> The youngest court is <b>the Court of Pride</b>. They tell the story of the Magic Brush, in which a poor but virtuous young man is granted the ability to paint anything he likes into existence. He uses this power to bring prosperity to his people, but when a cruel and greedy lord takes him captive and demands that he paint a mountain of gold, the clever peasant sees to it that he is destroyed by his own blind avarice. The court encourages charitable souls who take pride in doing good works for their community, and artists who take pride in the art they create. Although less concerned with accumulating wealth than the other courts of the Freehold, they are able to compete for power through their willingness to give away all that they have, keeping nothing for themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-14-2015, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T01:50:21-07:00","id":554054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=554032#post554032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's pretty far out, man... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I've been brainstorming ideas for a San Francisco Freehold; it's been observed before that the Bay Area seems well suited to being a setting for Changeling, and I live in nearby Santa Cruz, so I have a fair amount of familiarity with the area. Here's my basic idea; more to come soon, hopefully:<br /> <br /> <b>The Freehold of Gold Mountain</b><br /> <br /> San Francisco's freehold emerged in the waning years of the California Gold Rush, when the heady days of the 49'ers were already starting to fade into legend and the new city was settling into a modicum of stability. The first Changelings to emerge from the Hedge into the Bay Area were mostly recent arrivals who had been drawn to California by the promise of wealth and a better life, particularly poor Chinese immigrants whose relative invisibility made them easy prey for the Others. The name &amp;quot;Gold Mountain&amp;quot; is itself borrowed from the Cantonese <i>Gam Saan </i>(\u91d1\u5c71), and Chinese folklore has had a major impact on the structure and rituals of the freehold.<br /> <br /> Gold is the central metaphor around which the courts of Gold Mountain orient themselves, representing a whole host of physical and philosophical treasures which Changelings of the freehold seek. The highest law of the land is the Golden Rule, which states that &amp;quot;he who has the gold, makes the rules.&amp;quot; The Changelings of San Francisco hold periodic elections, during which each court nominates one of their own to be the leader of the Freehold as a whole. Candidates gain the support of rival courts by buying it; each makes an offer of some sort to those who would endorse them as ruler, and whoever makes the best offer is ushered into power - after they pay up, of course.<br /> <br /> Four courts vie jockey for power in the Freehold (though I haven't quite come up with names for them), each of which grounds its philosophy in a unifying narrative:<br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Greed</b> claims to be the oldest of the courts, and this may well be true. They tell the story of the Gold Rush itself, when brave men risked all in the pursuit of unimaginable wealth, and the most capable among them seized it and built legacies of power and prestige. Unapologetic capitalists and masters of the strange economy of the Fey, the court does not see greed as a sin, but rather a fundamental part of human nature that motivates people to compete and achieve, and in doing so build a better world.<br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Fellowship</b> tells the story of the Golden Nugget, in which a pair of true friends and hard workers refuse to bicker over a treasure that cannot be shared, and in the end are rewarded twofold. They stress the importance of pulling ones own weight, but also of helping out one's fellow Changeling, so that the community as a whole may know strength and prosperity.<br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Anger</b> tells the story of an outlaw, Joaquin Murietta, who is said to have lost his brother and wife to a drunken mob. After ruthlessly hunting down the men responsible and exacting his revenge, he took to robbing Anglo miners of their gold and distributing it to poor Mexicans struggling under the yoke of an unjust society. While many in the other courts challenge accuracy of this tale, the Court of Anger cares less about the historical Murietta than it does about his role as an archetype of righteous anger and and rebellion. They seek to embolden the poor and the powerless and stoke anger and resentment against the injustice of the status quo, and aren't above using violence and robbery as tools in pursuit of their goals.<br /> <br /> The youngest court is <b>the Court of Pride</b>. They tell the story of the Magic Brush, in which a poor but virtuous young man is granted the ability to paint anything he likes into existence. He uses this power to bring prosperity to his people, but when a cruel and greedy lord takes him captive and demands that he paint a mountain of gold, the clever peasant sees to it that he is destroyed by his own blind avarice. The court encourages charitable souls who take pride in doing good works for their community, and artists who take pride in the art they create. Although less concerned with accumulating wealth than the other courts of the Freehold, they are able to compete for power through their willingness to give away all that they have, keeping nothing for themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is...<br /> <br /> ...golden. /sunglasses","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T02:34:13-07:00","id":554076,"title":"","content":"<b>The Hollywood Freehold</b><br /> <br /> Few places are quite as invested in the <i>idea</i> of presenting stories as Hollywood; there's new movies coming out all the time, in every genre. And the Changelings of Hollywood use this ever changing collection of stories to confuse Huntsmen and Fae - the Courts of Hollywood change every six months. That's because the ritual performed is that of creating a movie and then having an awards ceremony: positions in the Court are handed out based on accolades. Freehold Approaches are based on the winning film, Court Approaches are based on the film being worked on, and personal approaches based on the role currently being played.<br /> <br /> Traditionally the director of the &quot;Best Film&quot; is the King or Queen - titled &quot;Producer&quot; - of the Freehold and non-honored cast and crew make up the bureaucracy; other honors such as Best Protagonist, Best Deuteragonist, Best Antagonist, Best Music, &amp;c receive other positions of power such as Champion or Enforcer.<br /> <br /> New Courts are formed amongst those with no official position at the beginning of each movie season (Summer for the Winter awards, Winter for the Summer), and courtiers are encouraged to move around and explore new avenues of expression, new roles, new costars, and new genres of film.<br /> <br /> The Summer movie season is upon us, and there are currently three competing courts:<br /> <br /> The Court of <i>My Life on Credit</i> - an introspective look on the dangers of modern consumerism and an over reliance on Goblin Contracts, <i>My Life on Credit</i> explores the existential weight of the debt cycle even if one has the ability to pay it off. (PG - moderate language) Emotion: Angst.<br /> <br /> The Court of <i>The Coldest Iron</i> - a semi-historical drama set in a European city that's being ruled by a True Fae, <i>The Coldest Iron</i> has enough character development, sex, and violence to wow any discerning moviegoer. (R - nudity, language, violence, gore). Emotion: Tension.<br /> <br /> The Court of <i>The Huntsmen Hunter</i> - when Thane Thorgron's boyfriend is taken across the Hedge by Huntsmen, Thane pulls out all the stops to get him back by becoming <i>The Huntsmen Hunter</i>. Not even the Hedge is tank resistant! (PG-13 - violence, explosions). Emotion: Excitement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T04:24:08-07:00","id":554140,"title":"","content":"We're doing Freeholds now?<br /> <br /> This one is for the archetypical USA small town.<br /> <br /> <b>The Anytown Freehold</b><br /> <br /> The Freehold claim that their fonders were born in the iron age, and they lived well and prospered for every generation the village would come togeather and choose the greatest of their number to be a king. They would obey their monarch in all things, and so each became as great as the village's best. But one king decreed upon his deathbed that they would choose his eldest son; for the king loved his son as all fathers do and could not see that his son was not the greatest in the village.<br /> <br /> Under the king's son's rule the village fell into poverty. The walls crumbled, the warriors became lazy and arrogant. The Gentry saw this weakness and took the entire population as slaves.<br /> <br /> By the time the survivors escaped the world they remembered no longer existed. &quot;Do not fear.&quot; they told one another,. &quot;We will find a king who understands this new world&quot;.<br /> <br /> Following power itself the arrived at Washington where they saw congressmen and senators going about their business. &quot;Surely one of these powerful men will be our king&quot; they said. But the senators and congressmen spoke about elections, and checks and balances, and the villagers could not understand them.<br /> <br /> Next they travelled to Boston, where they saw factories and industry on a scale they couldn't imagine. &quot;Surely a man who can create such marvels could be a king&quot; they said. But the industrialists spoke of shareholders, and investments, and capitol, and the villages could not understand them.<br /> <br /> Then they arrived at Pennsylvania, where they saw the university. &quot;These men have studied all things, surely one of them must know how to be a king&quot; they said. But the scientists spoke of methodology, and peer review, and the villagers could not understand them.<br /> <br /> Distraught the villagers wondered the streets, they feared that without a king to protect them their old masters would return. By change they came across a lover presenting flowers and this was a language they could understand, and so they asked the flowers to choose them a king.<br /> <br /> <b>Bulwark Ritual</b><br /> <br /> Once a year the courts oneiromancers create a dreamscape. In this dreamscape there is a road beset by trials. The road leads to a hall with an empty throne with a crown of white lillies upon it. The oneiromancers take the dream and divide it up between as many vessels as they can, but by tradition every changeling must have at least one vessel.<br /> <br /> On the appointed day each Changeling secrets their vessels into people's beds. Some trust chance and Wyrd, others spend months before the day choosing their champions. That night each mortal with a vessel dreams themselves onto the path, they face the trials, and the first to reach the throne and claim the crown becomes king or queen of the freehold. Everyone else awakes with no memory and a good night's rest.<br /> <br /> The trials themselves can be as easy or as challenging as the freehold wishes. Only two rules remain in force, the first is that no king or queen may ever know of or influence the selection process, they're told the flowers, that is to say the Wyrd, chooses. The second is that one trial must rule out any mortal with a connection to the Gentry or to a changing freehold.<br /> <br /> In some desperate years those have been the only trials, but most have many more. A trial so that the new monarch cannot be cruel. A trial to exclude fae-tocuhed (for who wants a king to send his knights to Arcadia?) The Freehold often comes up with lengthy and elaborate criteria, but they must be careful. If no mortal makes it past all the trials the Bulwark shatters for the next year. Even setting too many trials will cause mortals to wake up before completing the quest or failing at a task.<br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Balsam The Unyielding Flora, The Red Blossom, The Court of Stubbornness</b><br /> <br /> <i>I was subjected to tortures you mere mortals couldn\u2019t imagine so I\u2019d like some fucking sympathy please.</i><br /> <br /> The Court of Balsam do not return to mortal society so much as they expect mortal society to come to them on their terms. Almost every Changeling returns from Arcadia with phobias, supersitions and sometimes even frailties. The Court of Stubbornness doesn't even try to overcome these, they're offended by the notion that they should. Instead they mortal society to accommodate them. While the Freehold considers the Red Blossom to be stubborn gits who refuse to understand every relationship requires some give and take, they are invaluable to the Freehold because they remind the other changelings that yes, they do have issues, and yes they need to ask for accommodation before they snap.<br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Hollyhock The Proud Bloom, The Gold Blossom, The Court of Ambition</b><br /> <br /> <i>I\u2019m sure you\u2019ve read all sorts of faerie tales about our trickery, well that\u2019s the old way. Modern faeries understand the benefits of customer satisfaction. So here\u2019s my offer, seven years younger for seven million in cash, and I\u2019ll make the same offer in seven years time. </i><br /> <br /> The Court of Hollyhock want a life among mortals, but not just any life. Wealth, power or fame, their new life is going to be extraordinary if it takes every Contract they know to make it happen. This Court provides the Freehold with much of it's wealth and influence which makes up for the fact that the Gold Blossom is the least involved in day to day Freehold Life.<br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Honeysuckle The Choking Vine, The Pink Blossom, The Court of Dependency</b><br /> <br /> <i>Please, we can make it work. I can change.</i><br /> <br /> The True Fae break their slaves. Their souls are full of gaps, and the Court of Honeysuckle return to the mortal world looking for someone who can fill those gaps. Some seek out their old family or their old loves, others tumble through relationship after relationship always looking for &quot;the one&quot;. The Pink Blossom is infamous for the fragility of their members, especially when they're supressing their true personality for their lover's benefit, however the Choking Vine is invaluable to the Freehold because they're the only Court who, however clumsily, relate to average mortals on their own level.<br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Violet The Humble Herb, The Blue Blossom, The Court of Satisfaction </b><br /> <br /> <i>Hi Ho, Hi Ho, It\u2019s Off To Work We Go!</i><br /> <br /> If the Flower Courts are about fitting in with mortal society then the Court of Violet have figured it out. They find some quiet corner, usually one where their faerie talents are useful, and then they keep their heads down and do their job. Typically invisible, and happy that way, the Humble Herb take satisfaction in their work and being valuable to the mortals around them. In the Freehold the Blue Blossom are the ones who keep everything running. Few ever aim for status or influence, and those who have status or influence know better than to take the Court of Satisfaction for granted.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lily Crown The Royal Flower, The White Blossom, The Crown</b><br /> <br /> A pure white lily symbolises many things. It symbolises virginity and purity, a Changeling\u2019s lost state of grace before the Gentry plucked them from earth. To give someone a white lily says that it is heavenly to be with you, as it is heavenly for Changelings to be back home with humanity. Most importantly of all a white Lily symbolises majesty.<br /> <br /> The Lilly Crown belongs to one mortal a year. Even though the Freehold has some influence in their monarch, they still end up with an ignorant mortal suddenly discovering that they're king or queen of the faeries.<br /> <br /> None of the other Flower Courts have a Court Crown, their power is concentrated in the Lily Crown to grant a mortal everything they need to rule the faeries. The Crown provides:<ul><li>The Sight, Lily Kings can see through the Mask. (Former Kings retain this ability)</li> <li>Comfort with the Hedge: Lily Queens have a five die pool to open Hedge Gates and may open or create new ones by spending a point of Willpower. Once inside The Hedge they can navigate, are immune to any mental effect that does not affect Changelings and they are protected from both the thorns and transforming into a hobgoblin.</li> <li>The ability to make up to 5 Pledges, as well as Pledges of fealty and vassalage.</li> <li>Protection from magic: Any dice pool to activate a contract or which has been increased through magic takes a 5 Success penalty when targeting a Lily King, unless his majesty consciously allows it.</li> <li>Status in the courts, just as a Mantle provides social bonuses so does the Lily Crown. Lily Queens get a +3 bonus to all Flower Courts, which can stack with Court Goodwill to a maximum of +5. (Former Queens retain a +2 bonus and any Goodwill their previous subjects feel).</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-14-2015, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T05:53:12-07:00","id":554198,"title":"","content":"I am really loving what's coming out of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T10:12:38-07:00","id":554492,"title":"","content":"I'm getting thoughts on the courts/ideals/emotions of Paris. Could use some alternative takes on the Bulwark for inspiration.<br /> <br /> I think one thing I want to emphasize is the use of 'beauty' and 'ugly' to dress up and hide one another. Every rose has thorns, a beast may be kind, a family member may devour you. Paris is the city you go to fall in love in. Paris is the city you go to rise in hate in. That sort of thing.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I still want to keep elements of being betrayed by cynicism and rewarded by 'romance'* still, though. Thanks go to Ruby from The Path reminding me that there's a danger in wholly assuming a cyclical pattern between the two.<br /> <br /> *I need better words.<br /> <br /> EDIT: without context:<br /> <br /> Empathy/Caution-White Rose-Open/Expressive/Callous-???-The Closed Aerie-Songbirds, Distant-Pensiveness<br /> Love/Lust-Red Rose-Giving/Loner/Welcomed-???-The Ember Garden-Florists, Coal-eyed-Joy<br /> Patience/Haste-Blue Rose-Opportunistic/'Timely'/Finality-???-The Clear River-Steersmen,Punctual-Anticipation<br /> ?Protection?/Violence-Black Rose-Potential/Untouchable/Prepared-???-The Grave Hollow-Blackguards, Biters-Contempt<br /> Civilization/wilderness-Gold Rose-Knowledgable/Carnal/Dominating-???-The Sundown Spire-Pathfinders,Strays-Awe<br /> <br /> &quot;Go Deeper&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ooh, I should rewatch Hanna.<br /> <br /> Yes, this has become an open notes thing.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Note to self: The Maiden is not Disney's Belle. It is intended to be a potent and powerful icon that does not only emphasize the false idea that maternal qualities are the ideal for women. <i>The Maiden is the protagonist of this Bulwark, transforming and transformed, as much as any of the other roles, and is conventionally the one who decides whether it is tragic or comedic.</i><br /> <br /> Well, maybe not the Woodsman as much. The Woodsman is, after all, a concession to the True Fae, telling the Wyrd &quot;We can hunt our own, thanks, keep your Huntsmen away.&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm not sure how much to take away from the darkness of the Wild One. While the Wild One is the Wolf, it is also the Beast, and the beast is commonly kind-even Enkidu, straying from the template a little, is a more....not what you'd expect.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Then again, &quot;sweetest tongue hides sharpest tooth.&quot; THe Wild One is a character to navigate as much as shape. The dichotomy of the Beast and the Wolf and the mixed message from the two together more or less is a microcosm for Paris on the whole.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Gaulish Gods are not my speciality<br /> <br /> EDIT: I need to flesh them out, but approaches!<br /> <br /> White<br /> -----<br /> Hood-Trust a Stranger-Friend, the Huntsman gains a Yearning when they convince a courtier to trust them.<br /> Beauty-Look At the Surface, the Huntsman gains a Yearning when they trick a courtier in accepting the face-value.<br /> <br /> Red<br /> ---<br /> Hood-Dress in the Fire, the Huntsman gains a Yearning when he gets a courtier to hurt themselves in order to get what they want.<br /> Beauty-Beast Out of a Man, the Huntsman gains a Yearning when he drives someone to hurt the courtier out of love.<br /> <br /> Blue<br /> ----<br /> Hood-Come and Sleep, the Huntsman gains a Yearning when he tricks a courtier to miss something important in haste<br /> Beauty-Don't Abandon Us Tomorrow, the Huntsman gains a Yearning when he gets a courtier to delay fulfilling a promise.<br /> <br /> Black<br /> -----<br /> Hood-As It Used to Be, the Huntsman gains a Yearning when he catchs a courtier unprepared for them.<br /> Beauty-If You Run Away, the Huntsman gains a Yearning when he forces a courtier to rely on another for protection.<br /> <br /> Gold<br /> ----<br /> Hood-Listen to a Wolf, the Huntsman gains a Yearning when they trick a courtier into engaging a clearly dangerous situation.<br /> Beauty-Your Look is Burning, the Huntsman gains a Yearning when they manipulate someone into judging the courtier for indulging their wilder instincts.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Note to Self-<br /> <br /> Maiden wins Investigation(Wild One) and Occult(Woodsman).<br /> Wild One wins Persuasion(Maiden) and Subterfuge(Woodsman).<br /> Woodsman wins Brawl(Wild One) and Survival(Maiden).<br /> <br /> Or in other words,<br /> <br /> a Maiden/Wild One Union gives everyone +1 to Investigation and Persuasion,<br /> a Maiden/Woodsman Union gives everyone +1 to Occult and Survival,<br /> and a Wild One/Woodsman Union gives everyone a +1 to Subterfuge and Brawl.<br /> <br /> Sound about right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-29-2015, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T11:02:09-07:00","id":554583,"title":"","content":"Okay, here's my first crack at Court Creation. Its been home for the last three years. Abu Dhabi.<br /> <br /> **********************<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Step 1: Founding a Freehold's Story</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Alright, where to start? What is it that the desert wolves of </i><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><i>Ar Rub' al Khali say? Ah yes... This story is true. Except you know it fucking is, because you can see it all around you. Go to any bookstore, listen in any majilis and you will hear this tale of two boys. They may tell it a bit differently, but all of them are true. This is the tale of Shakhbut and Zayed. Its also the tale of Abu Dhabi. Both were brilliant young men, charming, faithful, well read and true Muslim poets, worthy each of being the Khalifas of old. When their uncle Saqr fell the bullets of a gunman, the title of Sheikh passed to the elder of the brothers, Shakhbut. Ruling for 38 years, Sheikh Shakhbut was all that the desert people of Al Ain and Abu Dhabi could desire in the time after the Great War. The Pillars of Islam were upheld and our way of life prospered, but those days did not last forever. They something under the sand dunes. Black gold. The Oil the British so craved, the very thing that made the Sauds so powerful was sitting under our land, waiting to be tapped, yet Sheikh Shakhbut would not allow it. He feared that to do so would be to end our way of life. Zayed say something else though. He saw what his brother couldn't and wouldn't. Times were changing, and unless our people changed with them, we would be lost to the desert forever.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Zayed would not have a return to the days of wars and feuds amongst his own family. He and the high council removed Shakhbut from power, but they did it bloodlessly with exile The former Sheikh would return within the decade and live our his life for another two. Now Zayed was Sheikh and he was only bound by his ambition. Overtures were made and in just five years, Abu Dhabi no longer stood along. Six other Emirates joined with them, none so powerful as Abu Dhabi's former rival, Dubai. Together, they forged themselves into a new nation that would stand together and prosper from their shared resources. Sheikh Zayed was no longer just Sheikh, or even High Sheikh of Abu Dhabi, and President of UAE. No, he was greater by far, he because Our Father Zayed, the Father of a Nation: The United Arab Emirates.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Why does our court focus on such a human story? Our Father Zayed may not have been supernatural, but the Wyrd respects those who make their own destinies. It was immediately clear to myself and the other Changelings who lived in the sand that we could use Zayed and Shakhbut's tales as our Bulwark. They were both amazing people. I wept for week in the sands when I heard of Our Father's passing in 2004. He was the man we needed to build ourselves a true nation. Ironically, it may be Shakhbut we need now, but we have lost forever. Many of his fears are becoming true. We have lost our tradition of pearl diving and now we are losing our Arabic language amongst our youths. It is the challenge that lies before our leaders. That is the way of the world though. It moves on. We can try and bring as much of the past with us as we can, but ultimately, we must move with it. I am confident they will keep us moving.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> -Abdulla bin Uthman bin Abdel, Imam of the Falcon Court</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Step 2: Building the Bulwark</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> The Bulwark of Abu Dhabi (which applies to the entire Emirate, not just the city of Abu Dhabi) is a series of monthly rituals that evoke both Zayed and Shakhbut. The first is both simple and sage. The Emir, head of the Courts of Abu Dhabi, must attend all five prayers on the three nights of the new moon at Sheikh Zayed Grand Mosque. This means that the Emir must Muslim, or convert to Islam prior to becoming Emir, so that he is permitted within the Mosque during prayers. The Mosque was Zayed's Magnum Opus, completed posthumously and above and beyond being the third largest mosque in the world, it is also a powerful and possibly unique location within the Hedge. It is almost tranquil there, as if the Eden Imagery from within the mosque as impacted the Hedge itself.<br /> <br /> The second half of the Bulwark is far more dangerous, both mentally and physically. During the Full Moon in the middle of each Islamic month, the Emir must hold a court within the Desert, far from civilization. This is a highly traditional Arabic affair, with one exception. Any being who knows of the event and possesses any manner of supernatural power is allowed to attend. This can range from the simplest child who can see ghosts to the utterly terrifying prospect of the True Fae themselves wandering out of the desert as Jinn. Most frequently though, it is an opportunity for the changelings to connect with the werewolves of the desert, who lead a far more rugged lifestyle. There is are also visits from the Unchained of Iran, Russia, and Canada, as well as the occasional Mummy. The Vampires never risk being caught in the desert sun. Part of the ritual is a pledge to defend the hospitality of the camp, and no one may partake unless they agree to it.<br /> <br /> ********************<br /> <br /> <br /> I've got more for the other parts, but I don't have time to type it now. More to come...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 06-14-2015, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T20:35:34-07:00","id":555163,"title":"","content":"The Courts of the Circus:<br /> <br /> These Courts were originally created by a band of wandering performers back in Europe. It's been long enough that even the oldest Courtiers aren't certain exactly who the creators were. There are stories of a band of motley Roma who gathered together in Romania after escaping from their Durances, a group of minstrels from France, or a Commedia Del'Arte troupe from northern Italy, and each has its believers. Wherever the Circus Courts began, they spread among wandering performers. There are several nomadic Freeholds based on these Courts, and while some are still circuses, there are also wrestling leagues and at least one Fae rock band whose tour personnel are made up of members of the Courts of Ring and Road. The Story this Freehold tells is that of the wandering band of strangers and rakes who appear in town amid fanfare and spectacle, who draw in those around them with merriment and astonishing displays, then disappear once the performance is done, possibly never to return.<br /> <br /> The Courts divide their rule based on whether the circus is in motion or has stopped for a performance. From the moment the first member of the troupe sees the first occupant of the place they intend to perform until the dawn after their final performance in a given venue, the Court of the Ring holds sway over the Freehold. From that dawn until the troupe arrives in a new city, the Court of the Road rules. The Ringmaster and Roadmaster of the troupe generally keep in close conversation, deciding on locations for performances, discussing safe routes through the Real or the Hedge, and dividing the jobs for the Freehold among the courts. While all members of the Ring Court perform on stage and all members of the Road Court have responsibilities offstage (such as ticket-taking or security work), members of each Court also often have duties in the other Court's bailiwick: For example, the whole of the Freehold helps to set up the circus in a new location, Ring and Road courtiers working in concert to set up their stages. Likewise, Road Courtiers often serve as assistants or stagehands for performance, and may also be pressed into service as clowns, chorus members<br /> <br /> The Circus Courts' Bulwarks are twofold. First, there is the tradition of wandering performance. A freehold troupe will never remain in a single location for longer than a fortnight, and will never travel for longer than a month before stopping to perform. The other Bulwark is a harder, and sometimes darker, affair. At least once a year, the troupe must take with them a young member of the community they've performed in to become part of their circus. Much of the time, this is simple - there have always been those who wished to run away from home, and the Circus Courts are happy to oblige. After a year as a hand in the circus (and often left utterly clueless regarding the nature of their circus-mates), the youth is generally disillusioned by the hard work and struggle of the circus life and is happy to wander away in peace - and those who remain are often Ensorcelled and become members in full standing in one of the Courts, holding nearly the same status as one of the Lost. When willing enlistees are unavailable, however, some Circuses are happy to take matters into their own hands, and either manipulate people to join or outright kidnap children to serve as virtual slaves beneath the canvas of their tents for a year. At the end of this time, some of these kidnapped youths are released. Others are never seen again.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><b>The Court of the Ring: the Court of Wonder, the Scarlet Robe</b></u></span><br /> The Wonder Court encompasses many of the performers of a traditional Circus Freehold. They believe in dealing with the trauma of their Durances by ignoring it, painting over it with the laughter and tears of their audiences. Despite a reputation for flightiness, Courtiers are generally incredibly hard-working, always testing a new routine, writing another song, or training their beasts to perform a brand new trick. That said, they play as hard as they work, if not harder, and there's a saying that if you see a Ring Courtier before noon the day after a show, it's because the husband came home early. Ring Courtiers approach new situations with unbridled optimism, enthusiasm, and curiosity. They find beauty and joy in the smallest things, and love nothing so much as to discover something or someplace new. They're not fools, however, and they often learn powerful magic with which to defend themselves. The Court of Wonder serves to remind their counterparts of the Road to take joy in life - they *have* escaped, and there is much beauty in the world, if you just look around to see it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><b>The Court of the Road: the Court of Worry, the Oaken Staff</b></u></span><br /> The Court of Worry, in contrast to their more colorful cousins, make up the administrative and technical staff of the circus. They cope with their Durances by careful consideration and planning of the future, accounting for dangers and trials that may come so that they can be prepared for whatever they may face. Road Courtiers tend to be dour, pessimistic sorts, but they often have a sense of wry, even gallows humor about their circumstances. After all, if the situation's as bad as it can get, at least it can't get any worse, right? The Court is split fairly evenly between nervous intellectuals and cautious brawlers, and more than a few members of the Court turn out to be much smarter than they first appear. The Road Court values mundane skill, considering it more reliable than unpredictable Fae magic, though divination is a prized exception. The Worry Court tempers their counterparts' enthusiasm, reminding them that dangers uncounted lurk in the World of Darkness, and that walking into strange places blindly is an easy way to lose life, mind, or freedom.<br /> <br /> Edit: Removed a word that I have learned, since writing this post, is a slur.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1168,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","user":"HobbitGuy1420","date":". 08-30-2023, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T20:36:53-07:00","id":555165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=554140#post554140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Court of Honeysuckle The Choking Vine, The Pink Blossom, The Court of Dependency</b><br /> <br /> <i>Please, we can make it work. I can change.</i><br /> <br /> The True Fae break their slaves. Their souls are full of gaps, and the Court of Honeysuckle return to the mortal world looking for someone who can fill those gaps. Some seek out their old family or their old loves, others tumble through relationship after relationship always looking for &quot;the one&quot;. The Pink Blossom is infamous for the fragility of their members, especially when they're supressing their true personality for their lover's benefit, however the Choking Vine is invaluable to the Freehold because they're the only Court who, however clumsily, relate to average mortals on their own level.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm having trouble picturing someone who would voluntarily join that Court with the negative way it's presented. I mean, dependent people don't usually self-identify as being dependent, do they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T00:38:31-07:00","id":555377,"title":"","content":"I think that new system brings great balance. There was a lot of talk how much easier changelings are now, and more complicated, but now, it is much harder to protect from True fae. before you just had to make sure there's no war and stay low. Now, if you don't complete Story, you get Keepers knocking at door.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6005-coolcat12345","name":"coolcat12345","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T01:25:16-07:00","id":555395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=555165#post555165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm having trouble picturing someone who would voluntarily join that Court with the negative way it's presented. I mean, dependent people don't usually self-identify as being dependent, do they?</div> </div> </div> </div>Trust or faith are easier ways to sell, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T01:28:33-07:00","id":555397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=555165#post555165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm having trouble picturing someone who would voluntarily join that Court with the negative way it's presented. I mean, dependent people don't usually self-identify as being dependent, do they?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Beast had no trouble admitting he was utterly dependent upon Belle to break his curse <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T03:25:24-07:00","id":555438,"title":"","content":"Freehold of Ottawa.<br /> <br /> The National Courts, are based around the political parties of Canada. <br /> <br /> The Oragne Court- Changelings who support the NDP, Unionism, Collectivism, Socialism,.and Social Democracy, Feminism. They're Court Emotion is Compassion. The Orange Court is lead by NDP leader Tom Mulcair, who has the nickname the Grizzily, turns out he really was one, he's the Beast Seeming.<br /> <br /> The Red Court- The Court of Moderation, the Court of Liberal Party, the Centre, Tolerance, Liberalism, the Charter of Rights. Its Court Emotion is calm. Its leader is Stephen Harper, the REAL STEPHEN HARPER, who was horrified when his fetch became the Tory Prime Minister.<br /> <br /> The Blue Court- The Court of the CPC, of Tradionalism, of Libatarionism, of Capitalism, of Tax Cuts. The Emotion of the Blue Court is Rage. Its Leader is Former Senator Hugh Seagul.<br /> <br /> The Green Court- The Court of.the Green Party, Enviromentalism, Democractic Reform. Its Emotion is Concern. Its ruled over by David Suzuki. <br /> <br /> The Bloc used to form another court, but when the NDP ascended in Quebec, the Light Blue Court decided to Seperate and form they're own Freehold (with the Anglophone, Francophone, and Allophone Courts), although they demand the right to continue using the Ottawa Freeholds Currency, Standing Army, and Penisons.<br /> <br /> The Bulwark of the Ottawa Freehold, aka the National Freehold, is particapation in Mortal Elections,.during every Federal Election the Ottawa Freehold Particapates, each Court fighting for the Party it represents. The Mortal Election decides who leads the Freehold until the next election. Its an usual long time between rituals, but the ritual is long and invovled and often involves large sacrifices of cash. <br /> <br /> A unusaul trait of the National Bulwark is that the National Courts can extend it to visiting Changelings from other Freeholds, except the Bloc Freehold, all they need is Court Goodwill with one of the National Courts (and only one). Those Changelings use Court Goodwill instead of thier Mantle when defending against the True Fae. This makes Ottawa a Hub of InterFreehold Diplomancy and Interactions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T08:13:12-07:00","id":555707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=555397#post555397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Beast had no trouble admitting he was utterly dependent upon Belle to break his curse <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the Beast. Cocteau and earlier interpretations had him make it clear he was hoping Belle would break the curse, but he also maintained dignity and autonomy by not pressuring her.<br /> <br /> Disney's Beast, love him as I might, is a bit of a blubbering man-child.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-15-2015, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T14:35:14-07:00","id":556091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=555438#post555438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Red Court- The Court of Moderation, the Court of Liberal Party, the Centre, Tolerance, Liberalism, the Charter of Rights. Its Court Emotion is calm. Its leader is Stephen Harper, the REAL STEPHEN HARPER, who was horrified when his fetch became the Tory Prime Minister.</div> </div> </div> </div>LoL. I really did laugh at this one. Very cool idea...unfortunately it is incorrect. I knew him in the early 1990s while he attended U of C and before he joined Reform (really I did). If his Fetch is now PM, the Fetch took him a looooong time ago. ;-)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6475-xiaolung","name":"xiaolung","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T15:49:12-07:00","id":556161,"title":"","content":"Just need to settle on emotions, and I'll have more to pitch","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T17:04:07-07:00","id":556227,"title":"","content":"Alright, here's the first of the courts I've been developing for the Gold Mountain Freehold, the Court of the Mint (sorry for the wall of text &gt;_&gt;):<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>The Court of the Mint, the </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><i>Soeng</i></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>, the Court of Greed</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u201cI know what it\u2019s like to have nothing, and if there\u2019s one thing I\u2019ve learned it\u2019s this: there\u2019s no nobility in poverty.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In 1848, a newspaper editor named Samuel Brannon strode through the streets of San Francisco, holding aloft a vial of gold dust and shouting a proclamation that would change the history of a nation. \u201cGold!\u201d he cried, \u201cGold from the American River!\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Of course, by the time he made his proclamation, Brannon had already bought up all the picks, shovels, and pans he could find, and established what would be, for a time, the only store between San Francisco and the gold fields.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Brannon\u2019s proclamation resounded across the globe, and by 1949 men were flocking to California from around the globe, risking everything for the promise of wealth and a better life. Many found what they were looking for, but in the end it was men like Brannon, the shrewd and the ruthless, who profited most. It was men like Brannon who built San Francisco, as they have built all of the great cities and mighty empires of the modern age. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Court of the Mint claims to be the oldest of the Gold Mountain Courts, and it may very well be true. They take their name from the Old San Francisco Mint, which once was home to more than a third of the U.S. gold reserve and is one of the few notable buildings that survived the great earthquake of 1906. When the fires that followed reached the building, the windows melted and the very stones burst from the heat.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The day was saved through the heroic efforts of the workers trapped inside, who drew water from a well in the Mint\u2019s open-air courtyard and used it to cool the walls of the vault. In doing so they saved not only themselves, but the precious gold that was needed to back the nation\u2019s currency. The Court of the Mint points to this as but one example of how selfishness and the love of wealth can inspire humanity to greatness.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Courtiers of the Mint are capitalists, first and foremost. They see themselves as merchants and financiers, and can be linked in one way or another with nearly every legitimate money-making venture in the Bay Area (not to mention many less than legitimate ones). Their pursuit of wealth doesn\u2019t end with mere dollars and cents, however; it defines their relationship with the world of the fae as well. To them, Pledges simply represent another kind of business deal, and they can bargain like no others when the Goblin Market comes to town.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Arcadia really isn't so different from the world of finance, after all. Both are governed by arcane rules and elaborate contracts. And if there\u2019s one thing the Courtiers of the Mint know how to do, it\u2019s negotiate a contract.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Nickname:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> 49\u2019ers</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Approaches</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Bad Investment: </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Some accuse the Courtiers of the Mint of being misers, but they see themselves more as builders, creating new jobs and institutions by investing their money wisely. Huntsmen gain a point of Yearning when they successfully sabotage a business venture initiated or financed by a Courtier of the Mint.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Fool\u2019s Gold:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> A wise man once said that the problem with money is that it makes you do things you don\u2019t want to do. Huntsmen gain a point of Yearning when they entrap a Courtier of the Mint using the promise of money or other valuables as bait.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Let\u2019s Make a Deal\u2026:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Courtiers of the Mint have a hard time passing up the opportunity to wheel and deal, and are most vulnerable to those who can best them at their own game. Huntsmen gain a point of Yearning when they trick a Courtier of the Mint into accepting an exchange of goods or services that leaves them poorer or more vulnerable.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Trappings of Nobility</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Courtiers of the Mint bedeck themselves in symbols of prosperity, but always seek to present the appearance of professionalism and respectability. Collared shirts, tailored suits in dark colors, and Italian shoes make up the typical uniform of the Court. Courtiers are rarely seen without at least one piece of gold jewelry, but it\u2019s considered crass to overdo it. Rings are common, as are gold watches and simple earrings and necklaces (for women). The color most associated with the court is green; members of the court commonly wear ties in shades of green, while green shirts and dresses are often seen on courtiers outside of a professional setting. Other symbols of the court include coins (particularly the California gold coinage minted in the 19th century), gold dust, gold pans, picks, shovels, weighing scales, the Chinese characters \u5546 (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>soeng</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> \u201ccommerce; merchant\u201d) and \u8ca1 (</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>coi</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, \u201cwealth\u201d), and, of course, representations of the Old San Francisco Mint itself.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Rituals</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Feast of the Annunciation (March 2): </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The name of this annual festival is actually a somewhat sacrilegious pun. Unrelated to the Catholic solemnity of the same name, it instead commemorates Samuel Brannon\u2019s famous announcement of the discovery of gold at Sutter\u2019s Mill. On the day of the ritual, the President of the Court hosts a formal banquet, to which all members of the Court (and </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>only</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> members of the court) are invited. The President is expected to be a generous host - a disappointing Feast is thought to portend dark times for the Court. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The most important part of the ritual comes at the conclusion of the banquet: after offering a toast to the continued prosperity of the court, the President makes a pledge to contribute in some way to the continued growth and prosperity of San Francisco or the greater Bay Area in the time before the next Feast. After the President makes his pledge, each guest in attendance is expected to do the same. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">These pledges need not be altruistic in nature (and, in fact, rarely are); pledges to renovate a place of business or invest in a local start-up company are fairly standard. The pledge doesn\u2019t need to involve a huge monetary commitment, either, though making ostentatious pledges is one way to impress the Court\u2019s leadership. Failing to honor a pledge, however, is considered a dire sin indeed, with possible punishments up to and including expulsion from the Court.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Mint Day (April 18): </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Held at the Old Mint building itself, this ritual commemorates the earthquake of 1906 and the heroic effort of the mint worker on that day. It\u2019s an occasion for remembering fallen comrades and celebrating past victories. The event tends to begin on a somber note, but as the wine flows and the evening wears on it typically develops into an occasion for drunken boasts and humorous stories. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Market Day (late spring/early summer): </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Court of the Mint has a standing agreement with a mobile Goblin Market that sweeps into San Francisco each year with the summer fog. On the first day that the Market opens, only members of the court are to be permitted inside. However, on that day every Courtier must make at least one purchase. Members of the Court have a tradition of hosting parties on the evening following the market, where they boast about the deals they\u2019ve made and mercilessly mock fellow Courtiers who got taken for a ride.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Titles</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>President (Mantle 5):</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The highest title within the Court, the President is selected by the Elders from among those Courtiers with a sufficiently advanced Mantle based on his or her skills in leadership and bargaining. The President is usually a lifetime appointee, but the Elders of the Court can depose him by a vote of no confidence</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Elder (Mantle 4+):</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Sometimes also called \u201cSenior Partners,\u201d or simply \u201cPartners,\u201d Elders are respected members of the Court who have abundantly proven their ability and commitment to the ideals of the Court. The title of Elder is only conferred by unanimous agreement on the part of the existing Elders of the Court. Other members of the Court look to the Elders for guidance, and Presidents and Vice Presidents of the Court are often (but not always) also Elders.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Vice President (Mantle 3+):</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Originally, the Court of the Mint had only one Vice President, who was the highest-ranking advisor to the president and his appointed successor should he die or otherwise be rendered unable to govern the Court. In keeping with modern trends in business administration, however, there are now a variable number of Vice Presidents appointed by the President to oversee specific facets of the court. These include the Vice President of Human Resources (in charge of approving new recruits and monitoring the overall morale of the Court), the Vice President of Public Relations (charged with maintaining positive relations with the other courts, as well as keeping tabs on them), and the Vice President of Security (the chief military leader of the court).</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Officer (Mantle 2+):</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Sometimes also called \u201cSecretaries\u201d or even \u201cExecutive Assistants,\u201d Officers of the Court are Courtiers who have been entrusted with special duties by the President or a Vice President. Most Courtiers compete eagerly for these appointments, as being entrusted with official duties is usually the first step on the path to becoming an Elder of the Court.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Stakeholder (Mantle 1+):</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> \u201cStakeholder\u201d is an informal term sometimes used to refer to any accepted member of the Court who has no formal title. It is meant as a term of respect, recognizing that fact that even the lowest-ranking members of the Court contribute to its strength and survival.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Mantle of the Mint</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022 </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The mantle may manifest as a faint sound of jangling coins as the Courtier moves or the scent of freshly-printed dollar bills.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The character develops an almost instinctual grasp of the art of the deal, gaining a dot of Persuasion.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022 Courtiers gain a dot of the Goblin Vow merit related to the court.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022 A Courtier\u2019s mantle may cause her irises to shine like gold or emeralds, her hands to appear stained with green ink, or even manifest as the familiar ring of an opening cash register.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The character has no patience for mind tricks; if someone wants him to do something for them, they had better be prepared to pay for it. He gains the Indomitable merit.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Courtiers gain a Personal Approach related to how they fulfill the ideals and story of the court. Huntsmen cannot gain Yearning from a Court Approach unless they fulfill the Personal Approach first.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 The mantle is even stronger. The distinctive reek of cash clings to the character at all times, and she seems somehow surrounded by opulence no matter where she goes. Objects she holds or examines seem suddenly more valuable and desirable than they formerly appeared. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">New opportunities seem to positively throw themselves at the character, and he may distribute three dots between Contacts, Allies, Resources, or Retainers, which manifest through seemingly ordinary means shortly after this level of mantle is reached. Furthermore, as long as the character operates or remains invested in a money-making enterprise, he may experience a sudden and well-timed windfall once per story, sufficient for a single purchase of up to Resources \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-15-2015, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T19:37:14-07:00","id":556391,"title":"","content":"Do we have any sort of mechanic for Bulwark creation and what is suitable for ease of Bulwark and how often it should take place? I know we have some examples and that Freeholds with the Seasonal Court mechanic hand over control to the next Court every three months (give or take) to confuse and befuddle the True Fae... Though when I build up a Freehold (I'm considering the Story, though I have some gestating as I'm considering a Freehold set somewhere in the Severn Valley of Cthulhu Mythos fame), I would love to have the Bulwark be balanced with that.<br /> <br /> As far as a Court is concerned... I'm 100% making up a custom one for my character, having an Approach where the Huntsmen challenges him through the Dreamscape or Hedge, as I love playing Oneiromancers and I want to do more with those mechanics. Thats a start for Approaches for an Oneiromancer-based Court, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T21:34:02-07:00","id":556510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=554492#post554492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm getting thoughts on the courts/ideals/emotions of Paris. Could use some alternative takes on the Bulwark for inspiration.<br /> <br /> I think one thing I want to emphasize is the use of 'beauty' and 'ugly' to dress up and hide one another. Every rose has thorns, a beast may be kind, a family member may devour you. Paris is the city you go to fall in love in. Paris is the city you go to rise in hate in. That sort of thing.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I still want to keep elements of being betrayed by cynicism and rewarded by 'romance'* still, though. Thanks go to Ruby from The Path reminding me that there's a danger in wholly assuming a cyclical pattern between the two.<br /> <br /> *I need better words.<br /> <br /> EDIT: without context:<br /> <br /> Empathy/Caution-White Rose-Open/Expressive/Callous-\u00e9tranger, The Stranger Court-The Closed Garden-Gardeners,Porcupines-<br /> Love/Lust-Red Rose-Giving/Loner/Welcomed-c\u0153ur,The Heart Court-The Radiant Pyre-Pyrographers, Coal-eyed-<br /> Patience/Haste-Blue Rose-Opportunistic/'Timely'/Finality-temps,The Time Court-The Clear River- Water-bearers,Punctual-<br /> ?Protection?/Violence-Black Rose-Potential/Untouchable/Prepared-armes,The Arms Court-The Grave Hollow-Blackguards,Trippers-<br /> Civilization/wilderness-Gold Rose-Knowledgable/Carnal/Dominating-fronti\u00e8res,The Boundaries Court-The Sundown Spire-Pathfinders,Wanderers-<br /> <br /> &quot;Go Deeper&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ooh, I should rewatch Hanna.<br /> <br /> Yes, this has become an open notes thing.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Note to self: The Maiden is not Disney's Belle. It is intended to be a potent and powerful icon that does not only emphasize the false idea that maternal qualities are the ideal for women. <i>The Maiden is the protagonist of this Bulwark, transforming and transformed, as much as any of the other roles, and is conventionally the one who decides whether it is tragic or comedic.</i><br /> <br /> Well, maybe not the Woodsman as much. The Woodsman is, after all, a concession to the True Fae, telling the Wyrd &quot;We can hunt our own, thanks, keep your Huntsmen away.&quot;<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm not sure how much to take away from the darkness of the Wild One. While the Wild One is the Wolf, it is also the Beast, and the beast is commonly kind-even Enkidu, straying from the template a little, is a more....not what you'd expect.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Then again, &quot;sweetest tongue hides sharpest tooth.&quot; THe Wild One is a character to navigate as much as shape. The dichotomy of the Beast and the Wolf and the mixed message from the two together more or less is a microcosm for Paris on the whole.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Gaulish Gods are not my speciality</div> </div> </div> </div>The flower courts seem a litle abstract and disconnected from the Freehold's story. Have you considered basing the courts off of the key rolls in the Bullwark instead? Here's my thoughts on your Freehold; perhaps something like this:<br /> <br /> The city was once home to two different, warring, Freeholds, each based off one of the two stories (Beauty and the Beast and Little Red Riding Hood). Members of both courts joined together and founded the Court of the Daughter, modeled after the young girls from each story, then convinced the Changelings of each freehold to strike a truce and unite against some greater threat. When the Freeholds joined and the stories were merged, members of the Little Red Riding Hood based Freehold started the Hatchet Court, after the woodcutter from the tale. The courtiers who had followed the story of The Beauty and the Beast formed the Beastly Court. <br /> <br /> <b>The Hatchet Court</b> <br /> The Hunters, Wolfslayers, Woodsmen, The Iron Axe<br /> Emotion: Hatred (Sometimes justified, other times... not so much.)<br /> The Hatchet prides itself on it's fighting prowess, it's self-reliance, and it's knowledge of the local area (especially the Hedge). They endeavor to protect the Freehold from all manner of monsters, from hedge creatures to vampires. Unfriendly Changelings see them as arrogant, violent bigots who shoot first and ask questions later.<br /> Approach: Use their arrogance; make them underestimate their opponent.<br /> <br /> <b>The Beastly Court</b><br /> Lonely Ones, The Rose Court, The Court of Claws, Wild Ones<br /> Emotion: Anticipation (The Beast and the Wolf are both patient, in their own ways.)<br /> The Beastly Court (made up predominantly of Beasts, Ogres, and Darklings) likes to keep to itself. Their organization is loose and their meetings infrequent, to allow their members the privacy they crave. They dislike politics and niceties and are sometimes uncouth, yet they fancy themselves dignified and pride themselves on hospitality. When they do make friends, they are fiercely loyal - frighteningly so. When angered they are powerful enemies who should be feared for their cunning as much as their, often considerable, strength. Enemies see them as deceitful monsters, dressing up in sheeps clothes to lure innocents to their doom.<br /> Approach: Cause them to drive their own friends away.<br /> <br /> <b>The Court of Daughters</b><br /> The Golden Key, the Ring and Mirror, The Red Hoods<br /> Emotion: Courage (To go into the woods alone is bravery, as is standing beside someone that others hate.)<br /> The Daughters unified the courts and deserve full credit for founding the freehold, and they are the central element of the Bulwark, though they rarely rule. They prize the virutes of courage and compassion, as well as skepticism and caution. They often inspire a protective instinct in those around them. Those who dislike them see them as naive children lost in the woods.<br /> Approach: Earn their trust and feign weakness, taking advantage of their naivete and compassion.<br /> <br /> <b>The Bulwark</b><br /> The story changes slightly every year, depending on how the Bulwark plays out, but the roles are always the same: a maiden (the gender is fluid, but the term is used as a reference to both source stories), a monster who desires her, and her rescuer. The Bulwark is a complex sort of courtly game (with lots of dueling).<br /> <br /> The Courts hold a series of contests (usually duels), to determine the courtiers who will fill the rolls. The winner of each court takes a role as appropriate.<br /> <br /> At the outset, the monster (Wild One) and the rescuer (Woodsman) each choose a token (rose for the hero of the story, a thorn dripping blood for the villain). This determines their role in the Bulwark this year. It is not random; they choose deliberately. They cannot reveal their choices to each other. They may choose the same token. (So, you might have two heroes or two villains).<br /> <br /> In the first stage, the maiden goes to meet the monster in the forest (sometimes this is a literal forest, other times the hedge or somewhere else dangerous and remote), where the monster will attempt to convince her of its good intentions.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the rescuer must track the monster/find the maiden.<br /> <br /> When the rescuer arrives, the maiden must choose a side.<br /> <br /> If the party she chooses is a villain, she is &quot;captured&quot; by them. The other party must then defeat her captor, to secure her release.<br /> <br /> If the party she chooses is a hero, then the third party's token is revealed. If they are also a hero, the conflict is over, and the maiden will rule for the next year.<br /> <br /> If the winner of the duel between monster and rescuer is a villain, then the winner of their duel must face the maiden in a final duel, unless she relents. If she wins, she rules the Court for the following year. If she loses, she becomes The Captive Maiden and must serve the winners ruling Court for a year, and the Daughters find themselves politically disadvantaged for a year.<br /> <br /> If the maiden wins the contest in any way, the Court of any &quot;heroes&quot; is honored and shown favor by The Court of Daughters while they rule. <br /> <br /> If a &quot;hero&quot; wins the contest, the &quot;villain&quot; is barred from the freehold for a year and a day, and their court is unlikely to be treated favorably. While the maiden becomes The Beloved, a valuable advisor to the Freehold monarch with special privileges, and the Daughters are generally treated favorably throughout the year.<br /> <br /> If a &quot;villain&quot; wins the contest, the defeated monster or rescuer is barred from the freehold for a year. (The maiden becomes The Captive Maiden as above.) Traditionally, a &quot;villain&quot; will rule with an iron fist and rarely grant favors to other Courts, furthering his or her own Court's goals as much as possible during the year.<br /> <br /> This is a little complex and could probably use a flow chart. I like it because it provides a dilemma. If you choose hero, you are most likely to benefit politically, but you run the risk of just handing the crown to the maiden and you <i>could</i> still get royally screwed if the other side has played a villain and won. If you play a villain, you don't run the risk of the maiden getting to rule without a fight, and you're beholden to noone when you rule, but you risk making political enemies.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T21:42:50-07:00","id":556524,"title":"","content":"Just a note: iirc, maiden used to refer to virgins of both genders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T21:55:29-07:00","id":556534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=556524#post556524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a note: iirc, maiden used to refer to virgins of both genders.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I did not know that. Very interesting. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T21:57:10-07:00","id":556535,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm working on a set of three courts based around the three major Norns or Norse mythology. Hopefully, I'll be posting that in a day or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T00:47:54-07:00","id":556657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=556510#post556510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The flower courts seem a litle abstract and disconnected from the Freehold's story. Have you considered basing the courts off of the key rolls in the Bullwark instead? Here's my thoughts on your Freehold; perhaps something like this:</div> </div> </div> </div>How much of this post is a response to me and how much is a response to ArcaneArts?<br /> <br /> But anyway; in Toronto only the Court of Brass is directly tied to the Freehold's story. In Anytown only the Lilly Crown is directly tied to the Freehold's story.<br /> <br /> However the Freehold's Story does directly tie the lost to mortal humanity, and all the Flower Courts are about how it's members relate to mortal society. That's the core concept.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T01:29:43-07:00","id":556674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=556657#post556657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much of this post is a response to me and how much is a response to ArcaneArts?<br /> <br /> But anyway; in Toronto only the Court of Brass is directly tied to the Freehold's story. In Anytown only the Lilly Crown is directly tied to the Freehold's story.<br /> <br /> However the Freehold's Story does directly tie the lost to mortal humanity, and all the Flower Courts are about how it's members relate to mortal society. That's the core concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the confusion. That comment was intended for ArcaneArts. Hadn't considered that it might be taken to mean your botanical courts, too. Should have said Rose Courts not Flower, I suppose.<br /> <br /> I know the Courts don't all have to tie directly to the Freehold story, I just thought it would be neat if they did in ArcaneArts's concept. Just a suggestion, obviously.<br /> <br /> By the way, I really love the idea of the Freehold Monarch being a hapless mortal. I may steal that for a game at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5910,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","user":"CSSchulz","date":". 06-16-2015, 04:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T08:15:23-07:00","id":556905,"title":"","content":"First of all, I just want to say: Damn, I like your take Schulz!<br /> <br /> Second, that said, I wanted to avoid a deliberate one-to-one on the roles and the courts. I wanted it so that the Maiden, Wild One, and Woodsman could come from any court rather than having each one be a churning out of sanctified actors for each. I also wanted to make it more about the Courts to be commentaries on and interpretations of the story, creating conflict when those ideas of what a Maiden or a Woodsman is supposed to be while at the same time using them to sharpen one another, and finally have each one be a declaration of what each Lost feels in a focus in their life to keep from returning to Arcadia(The Rose Gate/The Treasure Hold of Diana/Grandmother's House[well, none of them exactly]). As an example not in the notes, the Blue Rose Court's priority of time comes from a relation of time to Clarity, both as a flaw and a virtue, the idea that knowing when and how to be patient and hasteful gives the insight and action neccessary to avoid the traps of the fae, where misapplication of both leads to capture. Stuff like that.<br /> <br /> This isn't a critique of your design, because again yours is <i>really</i> good, actually. I just wanted to go a different route. I feel like this evokes a greater sense of placed conflict within the freehold while also being more applicable to changelings <i>not</i> vying for the roles while at the same time making it more likely that someone not interested in the role could still get dragged in inadvertently. Doing that also gave the duels as a mechanic a bigger place in the story of the freehold, as each courtier is essentially telling another one, underneath every other pretense, &quot;You're doing it wrong&quot;, which, as anyone who has seen arguments between people with trauma can attest to, leads to some interesting dynamics.(Some good, some bad)<br /> <br /> But as a model for what I'd do if I had gone with my gut for the role-based courts, yours is what I would have wanted it to turn out as.<br /> <br /> (there's more to my logic, but I got work to do)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T13:32:01-07:00","id":557269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=556674#post556674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, I really love the idea of the Freehold Monarch being a hapless mortal. I may steal that for a game at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who said hapless <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> They're mortal, but that usually means they're saner than changelings - and if the bulwark ritual is done right you'd get someone competent.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T15:46:50-07:00","id":557462,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">The Freehold of the Free and Brave</span></div> <br /> <b>1 - What is the Tale?</b><br /> <br /> &quot;We stand for Uncle Sam, my friend - our story is the story of the Constitution, of the land of the free and the home of the brave. Not the way it <i>is</i>, a big mass of hypocrisy; no, we're the story good citizens feed to their kids - and it's a powerful one. If you work hard, and stay honest, you can <i>be someone</i>. The world doesn't care where you come from, only where you're going. It's the story that drew millions to our shores, and it's the story we echo in our movies, TV, and history books.<br /> <br /> We've got the American Dream at our back - let the Gentry come.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>2 - What's the Bulwark?</b><br /> <br /> The Freehold has wrapped itself in the cycle of Election; every two years, the Congress is re-elected, and every four years, they elect a new President. As long as this cycle is unbroken, the Bulwark will hold. However, there is a quieter, more subtle side to the Bulwark - the Freehold must believe that they are working towards &quot;a more perfect Union&quot;. If there are problems, they have to work to solve them - they can't give up, and any betrayal by those in power shows how <i>weak</i> the Bulwark really is...<br /> <br /> <b>3 - And the Courts?</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Court of Wheat</span><br /> <i>Oh beautiful, for spacious skies, for amber waves of grain</i><i>, for purple mountain majesties above the fruited plains!</i><br /> <b>Emotion:</b> Generosity<br /> <b>Trappings:</b> A farmer's tan, the amber of ripe wheat, and the yellow of maize. Straw and a stooped back, with filthy fingernails. Pitchforks and tractors - a hound, a cow, and chickens.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Court of the Endless Roads</span><br /> <i>I remember listening to songs about trains and feeling the rush of wonder at the possibility that the world was infinite and accessible all at the same time</i>.<br /> <b>Emotion:</b> Wanderlust<br /> <b>Trappings:</b> Dust and raincoats; an upturned thumb and the stink of gasoline or coal. Weather-beaten clothing and worn-out shoes. The brown of mud and the red of a sunburn. A walking stick, an oil can, and the stub of a train ticket.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Court of Industry</span><br /> <i>&quot;When the agent for the steam drill company brought the drill here,&quot; said Mr. Miller, &quot;John Henry wanted to drive against it. He took a lot of pride in his work and he hated to see a machine take the work of men like him.&quot;</i><br /> <b>Emotion:</b> Perseverance<br /> <b>Trappings:</b> Callused hands and strong arms; bags under eyes and the smudge of coal. Hammers and wrenches - picks and shovels and somber songs. The black of coal and the grey of steel.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Court of the Homeless</span><br /> <i>Keep, ancient lands, your storied pomp! Give me your tired, your poor...</i><br /> <b>Emotion:</b> Hope<br /> <b>Trappings:</b> Tattered clothing, a child in your arms, a shine in your eye. The white of dust and the blue-grey of the sea. A foreign look - an honest look.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Court of the Musket</span><br /> <i>Freedom is the sure possession of those with the courage to defend it.</i><br /> <b>Emotion:</b> Courage<br /> <b>Trapping:</b> The green of fatigues; the red of blood. Guns and knives and flags - medals on the chest, drums in the air. Straight-backed and ordered; the look of a young recruit, and the face of an old veteran. <hr /><br /> That's what I've got. I'm a bit sad now.<br /> <br /> (For those of you who are curious, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NRnu_BH-Zf4\" target=\"_blank\">here's the source of the quote I used for the Court of the Endless Roads.</a>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T20:36:42-07:00","id":557781,"title":"","content":"Here's the second Gold Mountain court, the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1RbJURDEvwr52GF2GmkiXzSpHKh1KCoyakji5CJgtu_o/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Court of the Bridge</a>. I figured I'd just put it in its own doc, so that it doesn't take up so much space here. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T05:50:06-07:00","id":558124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=557269#post557269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who said hapless <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> They're mortal, but that usually means they're saner than changelings - and if the bulwark ritual is done right you'd get someone competent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hapless means unlucky. I think an ordinary mortal who suddenly gets dragged into the thick of Changeling politics, saddled with a ton of responsibility, and probably stuck squarely in the Gentry's crosshairs is pretty unlucky. <br /> <br /> It occurs to me that you'd have probably a couple dozen past monarchs just hanging around the Freehold. That's a weird Freehold dynamic that could be pretty interesting.<br /> <br /> If I end up using the mortal monarch idea, I'd probably end up doing something so that they aren't sticking around after their year. Maybe they rule entirely in their dreams, with the Court sovereigns meeting in the king or queens dreams, bringing along any subjects who need an audience. At the end of their reign, the dreams stop, and they're left none the wiser. Or, in a much darker scenario, at the end of the year the Court rulers sacrifice the monarch in the hedge to complete the Bulwark. Only the Court rulers know what happens, and they're pledge bound to secrecy. Everyone else in the Court thinks the monarch is taken somewhere awesome as a reward, like a tropical paradise. I'd probably go with the second option; I like dark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T12:44:28-07:00","id":558572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CSSchulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=558124#post558124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurs to me that you'd have probably a couple dozen past monarchs just hanging around the Freehold. That's a weird Freehold dynamic that could be pretty interesting.<br /> <br /> If I end up using the mortal monarch idea, I'd probably end up doing something so that they aren't sticking around after their year.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, but I'd just have them sign a pledge to stay back and not cramp the new monarch's style in exchange for something nice. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T15:59:40-07:00","id":558814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=558572#post558572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good point, but I'd just have them sign a pledge to stay back and not cramp the new monarch's style in exchange for something nice.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A pledge is definitely a good start. It would also need to include provisions for not betraying the Freehold and it would need to be renewed regularly. But what do you do if they refuse the pledge?<br /> <br /> I'd be more concerned with what their relationship to the Freehold is like. Are they expected to participate in the Freehold's activities? If not, are they allowed to? Does the Freehold protect former monarchs or do favors for them? If so, how much energy is dedicated to that? Is it like former Presidents, who get Secret Service protection long after leaving office? Who gets stuck being the Changeling Secret Service? Is it an honored and sought after position or is it a shit job pawned off on new Changelings? If not, what's to stop enemies they made while serving as ruler from coming after them when they're no longer in charge?<br /> <br /> And, on another note, what would the Freehold do if the dream selection process got them a mortal who really, really didn't want to be the King or Queen of a fairie community. &quot;You're joking!? That was just a dream! If I'd have known it was real, I never would've taken that crown! This is crazy!&quot; Hell, how often does a human monarch run away or kill themselves? What does the Freehold do to stop that? Does it break the Bulwark if it happens?<br /> <br /> Please don't take these as criticisms of the idea. I'm almost certainly going to use it at some point. I'm only thinking up all these questions because I like it so much. These issues aren't flaws in the premise, they're just interesting and awesome plot wrinkles that having a mortal monarch for a year at a time brings up. I just ike to try and work out all the angles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T16:06:33-07:00","id":558820,"title":"","content":"Just a question, what happens if a character already has a particular benefit(I was thinking Merits in particular) given by a level of Mantle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T17:14:54-07:00","id":558876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=558820#post558820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a question, what happens if a character already has a particular benefit(I was thinking Merits in particular) given by a level of Mantle?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sanctity of Merits, essentially. You get the old point refunded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T18:54:38-07:00","id":558963,"title":"","content":"(Freehold brief) The Gatehold<br /> Location: Louisiana State Prison (population 5100 prisoners, 1700 staff members)<br /> <br /> Story: The descent and ascent, the archetypal story of a hero descending into an underworld and then, eventually, forcing his way out,but at a mighty cost<br /> <br /> Bulwark: The Suffering - a member of each court is nominated every Solstice and Equinox, and they have to go through a painful endurance test. The last changeling standing wins.<br /> <br /> Courts:<br /> The Court of Stone - The court of perseverance, the court of the bloody-minded, the court of those who struggle through the realities of prison life and seek to make themselves more comfortable through domination.<br /> The Court of Chains - The court of resignation, the court of lifers, the court of those who will never taste the 'real world' again, as far as they are concerned. Seen as a strange mix of apathy and serenity.<br /> The Court of Keys - The court of hope, the court of new fish, the court of those who peer through the bars of their windows and know that one day they'll be free. they seem unconcerned with their surroundings, knowing them to be a temporary roadblock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T22:16:19-07:00","id":559072,"title":"","content":"I really like the idea of each court having a Godly name, preferably in relation to the old pagan gods that would have been involve in France's upbringing(the Celts, and in particular the Gallic gods), but I can't find neat parallels. Still love the idea of a Diana Court, but if I can't get the gods thing to work, then it'll be the [Color] Rose Court as the main name. Anyways, the following are brief pitches for the Rose Courts of Paris, not fully capturing their idealism, cynicism, or reasons for their interpretation. Still, should be good.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><i><u>???, The White Rose, the Court of Pensiveness, the Songbirds and Distant of the Closed Aerie</u></i></b><br /> Keep your friends close, your enemies closer, and yourself far away-This is the motto of the Closed Aerie, changelings who embrace the lessons of empathy and caution from the freehold's stories-Beauty learned to love the Beast by understanding him, and yet Little Red Riding Hood's compassion only earned her the belly of the wolf, and so she learned to be wary of those with sweet tongues. Courtiers of the White Rose as a result tend to become openly friendly and understanding, making friends and digging up secrets of all around them, while being reserved with their actual selves, and as such make for great investigators and movers in Parisian culture, knowing who needs to meet who and playing the social games well without giving leverage on themselves.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Ideal of the Roles</u></b><br /> The Maiden is marked by her <i>open-mindedness</i>, her willingness to consider ideas and engage in activities foreign to her, to give Beast, Wolf, and Woodsman their due. White Maiden Duels tend to include an element that forces the duelists out of their comfort zone to test their ability to move into new realms.<br /> The Wild One is marked by her <i>expressiveness</i>, her ability to communicate an idea or emotion convincingly to another, regardless of whether they actually feel strongly about it or not. White Wild One Duels tend to test the Lost's ability to be vulnerable or to give the wrong impression deliberately.<br /> The Woodsman is marked by her <i>callousness</i>, her emotional distance from the people around her. White Woodsman Duels push the participants to do things that would make lesser participants squirm with discomfort-after all, the Woodsman must kill all manner of creature, regardless of her own reactions to them.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Approaches</u></b><br /> Trust a Stranger-Friend- the Huntsman gains a Yearning when he or his allies convince a courtier to trust them.<br /> Look at the Surface- the Huntsman gains a Yearning when his trick a courtier in accepting the face-value.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u><b>???, The Red Rose, the Court of Joy, the Florists and Freudians of the Ember Garden</b></u></i><br /> Flowers don't bloom without care and fires don't grow without fuel, and so the Ember Garden makes men and beasts out of each other by seeding the Paris area with the dual lessons of love and lust from the freehold's stories-Beauty's love made a prince of the beast and an aggressor of her suitor, while Little Red Riding Hood's chosen path of the prostitute's needles tore her apart with wet teeth and the harsh lessons of messy maturity. Courtiers of the Red Rose didn't miss out on the passionate psychology in their stories, and so serve as psychologists and resource managers for the freehold so that everyone has what they need to live as well as the reasons to do so, pricking and burning themselves with others' wants to keep Paris a joyful place worth returning to.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Ideal of the Roles</u></b><br /> The Maiden is marked by her <i>charity</i>, her willingness to give what she has to others, whether it be time and attention to a Beast, answers to a Wolf, bread to a grandmother, or fairness to a Woodsman. Red Maiden Duels tend to push an element of sacrifice for others to see how far she'll go to bring joy to a person.<br /> The Wild One is marked by her <i>isolation</i>, her seclusion from others as a result of her passions both fair and foul, her hunger for flesh either out of a need to connect intensely or vain indulgence. Red Wild One Duels tend to include elements that provide insight into whether a freeholder is strong enough to keep their problems to themselves.<br /> The Woodsman is marked by her <i>acceptance</i>, her ability to be welcomed into any group and to be seen as a desirable creature to be around. Red Woodsman Duels often challenge the participants to get into increasingly closed-off circles as part of the resolution of their conflict.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Approaches</u></b><br /> Dress in the Fire- the Huntsman gains a Yearning when he gets a courtier to hurt themselves in order to get what they want.<br /> Beast Out of a Man- the Huntsman gains a Yearning when he drives someone to hurt the courtier out of love.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u><i>???, The Blue Rose, the Court of Anticipation, the Steersmen and Punctual of the Clear River</i></u></b><br /> To grasp time is to grasp a pure vision of Arcadia and her threats, and the Clear River master the hidden lessons of patience and haste from their stories to see situations with Clarity and act accordingly-Belle's patience allowed her to see the Beast for what he was, but was pushed too far by her sisters and nearly caused the death of the Beast, while Little Red Riding Hood was too hasty in both judging the wolf and her 'grandmother' in the dark, and too eager to dawdle on the way to the cottage. Keen analysts and planners, Courtiers of the Blue Rose tend to keep the freehold moving as it needs and uncover the truths to the mysteries of Paris, struggling against the flowing rapids of the clock which seeks to make them overspend or speed through their minutes<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Ideal of the Roles</u></b><br /> The Maiden is marked by her <i>opportunism</i>, her willingness to work with the time given her by others for her own intended purposes, whether it be time with the Beast or family or enjoying the walk through the woods. Blue Maiden Duels often have a strict time limit, forcing the duelists to make as much as they can out of a little thing.<br /> The Wild One is marked by her <i>timeliness</i>, her keen sense of how much time to make for herself and others, such as how many days a father has with his family before accepting death or distracting a young girl to have more time to setup a trap. Blue Wild One Duels often involve participants finding a way to get more time to do what they need to do.<br /> The Woodsman is marked by her <i>finality</i>, her ability to solidly and conclusively resolve conflicts and keep them from going on beyond her own actions. Blue Woodsman Duels demand that whatever a freeholder does, it ends the conflict in a single act.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Approaches</u></b><br /> Come and Sleep- the Huntsman gains a Yearning when he tricks a courtier to miss something important in haste.<br /> Don't Abandon Us Tomorrow- the Huntsman gains a Yearning when he gets a courtier to delay fulfilling a promise.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u><i>???, The Black Rose, the Court of Contempt, the Blackguards and Biters of the Grave Hollow</i></u></b><br /> In the end, all problems are solved with hurting one another, and the Grave Hollow sees it as their mission to prepare the freehold while standing at the gate, serving as bleak living lessons of protection and violence from their stories-the Woodsmen and Beasts of each story solve their problems and guard the interests of others and themselves by tearing others apart, and the Maidens learn from the harsh experience. The Black Rose Courtiers don't have the patience for an ill-prepared city, and so teach all members of the freehold to fend and stand up for themselves while they seek out the freehold's enemies, honing a careful and vicious disdain for everyone and everything to build a tough community and rend opposition without wasting sentiment.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Ideal of the Roles</u></b><br /> The Maiden is marked by her <i>potential</i>, untested though she may be-The Black Rose strain to dig up the blessing of Beauty as a growing actor in her world, and scorn Little Red Riding Hood for her wastefulness. Black Maiden Duels should show that the duelists can pick up new skills quickly, proving they might stand some chance.<br /> The Wild One is marked by her being <i>untouchable</i>, demonstrating prowess in putting walls between herself and her enemies, being unseen by them, and slipping from their knives and bullets. Black Wild One Duels are often arranged to cast a scornful eye on those who get affected by their opponents, skewed to build momentum for the one who hits his opponent where it hurts.<br /> The Woodsman is marked by her <i>preparation</i>, her having the skills and tools on handed needed to deal with anything and anyone at any time. Black Woodsman Duels endeavor to include unexpected curveballs to the fulfillment of the duel, seeing if the freeholders can protect themselves and others from the random whims of the fae and the world.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Approaches</u></b><br /> As It Used to Be- the Huntsman gains a Yearning when he catches a courtier unprepared for them.<br /> If You Run Away- the Huntsman gains a Yearning when he forces a courtier to rely on another for protection.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u><i>???, The Golden Rose, the Court of Awe, the Pathfinders and Strays of the Sundown Spire</i></u></b><br /> The riddle of the fae is the struggle between primordial instinct and advanced self-control, and the Sundown Spire explores all frontiers to bring forth fruits of understanding to the freehold as they reconcile the balance of wilderness and civilization within the freehold's stories-Beauty, Beast, and Avenant are civil creatures struggling with the rule of their primal inclinations, while Little Red Riding Hood dives into the natural world that wears the veneer of polite modernity. Both rangers and hortculturalists of the Hedge and avid scientists and sociologists of the real world, Courtiers of the Golden Rose bring in the cutting edge and most mysterious of resources to the freehold, alongside their knowledge and instincts and extreme contrarian obsessions.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Ideal of the Roles</u></b><br /> The Maiden is marked by her <i>knowledge</i>, her great capacity for memorizing facts and eagerness to know more things, being possessed of an education whether it's used to good effect or not. Gold Maiden Duels often demand that the participants know or learn something to resolve their issues with one another, some hidden element missing from the equation.<br /> The Wild One is marked by her <i>carnality</i>, potent hungers for fundamental desires that shape their lives, whether they struggle with it or use it as a lodestar. Gold Wild One Duels usually involve an element that displays a willingness to show temptation, if not to indulge in it, and having the stakes measured in part by the proof of their connection to the simple world.<br /> The Woodsman is marked by her <i>dominance</i>, her prowess at bringing her environment under heel, shaping cities, forests, and dreams to her desire. Gold Woodsman Duels include an element of forcing their opponent to do what they desire, forcing them onto their territory, either intellectually, socially, or physically.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Approaches</u></b><br /> Listen to a Wolf- the Huntsman gains a Yearning when they trick a courtier into engaging a clearly dangerous situation.<br /> Your Look is Burning- the Huntsman gains a Yearning when they manipulate someone into judging the courtier for indulging their wilder instincts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaand that's the nutshell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-19-2015, 01:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T23:23:27-07:00","id":559109,"title":"","content":"A bit of an update or expansion to my Gold Mountain Freehold, now that I've spent a while thinking (some might say obsessing) about it:<br /> <br /> <br /> At the core of the story of Gold Mountain is a simple idea: that wealth leads to a better life. Wealth, in this case, can mean literal money, but doesn't have to. It basically refers to everything that a person owns which could, at least theoretically, be bought, sold, traded, or stolen. During a Changeling's durance, they owned nothing - not even themselves. In escaping from Arcadia, they won back that much, and now they want more.<br /> <br /> Each of the Courts of Gold Mountain defines its place in the Freehold's story by answering two questions: how do they acquire wealth, and what do they do with it once they've got it?<br /> <br /> For the <b>Court of the Mint</b>, aka. the Court of Greed, the answer to both questions is the same: they invest. Whether they're merchants buying low and selling high or venture capitalists carefully choosing which start-ups to finance, they believe that the only correct thing to do with wealth is to use it to generate more wealth.<br /> <br /> The ideology of the <b>Court of the Bridge</b>, aka. the Court of Affection, dictates that wealth should be earned through hard work and dedication. It stresses, however, that true success requires cooperation, and so they share their wealth with those they trust and rely on, rather than squandering it on themselves.<br /> <br /> The Changelings of the <b>Court of the Dome</b>, aka. the Court of Anger, take wealth from those whom they feel are undeserving, particularly those who have used it to abuse those less wealthy than they. While they certainly keep some of what they take, they justify their actions by redistributing the wealth they appropriate to the poor and downtrodden.<br /> <br /> The <b>Court of the Tower</b>, aka. the Court of Pride, are socially-conscious visionaries who fit uneasily into the larger story of the Freehold, considering wealth a goal unworthy of pursuit. Nevertheless, they are often expert fund-raisers, or rely on the support of wealthy patrons to make their visions reality. They channel what wealth comes their way into making the world a better place, either through charitable works or by creating things of beauty in the pubic sphere.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Bulwark that guards the Gold Mountain Freehold relies on the principal that symbols and displays of prosperity and good fortune can ward off evil, including the Keepers themselves. It takes the form of an extravagant celebration hosted annually by the King on the first day of the Chinese New Year. Although the customs and symbols of that holiday form the backbone of the ritual, the four Courts put on all manner of grand entertainments and spectacles, both traditional and otherwise. The whole affair is an orgy of conspicuous consumption that celebrates all that is good in the new lives the Changelings have built since leaving Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Changelings from other Freeholds sometimes see the Gold Mountain Bulwark as trivial compared to their own, more onerous traditions, but they miss the dangers and costs concealed under the merriment. Firstly, the cost of hosting the celebration is always enormous, and all but the most wealthy Kings must rely on generous donations from his Court to cover the expense. More than one King has been forced to abdicate when it became apparent that he wasn\u2019t going to be able to provide a sufficiently extravagant party.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the Gold Mountain Bulwark ritual is always held in a clearing of the Hedge. While this keeps the festivities away from the prying eyes of mortal authorities, it renders the event particularly susceptible to disruption by agents of the Keepers or other dangers of the Hedge. One might imagine that the attendees, anticipating the possibility of a raid, would refrain from excessive drink or other activities that would render them less able to defend themselves, but such restraint would defeat the purpose of the ritual.<br /> <br /> Finally, the Bulwark demands that the Changelings in attendance give themselves over fully to the revelry, which usually requires them to act counter to their nature. Courtiers of the Mint spend frivolously to bedeck themselves with fine clothes and jewelry, and distribute extravagant gifts without expecting anything in return. Courtiers of the Bridge leave their mortal friends and loved ones behind, and must selfishly accept whatever is offered to them. Courtiers of the Dome set aside old grudges (at least for a while), and cavort with misers and idle dilettantes. Courtiers of the Tower engage in debauchery and excess, and cast aside all shame and restraint. Although they may enjoy themselves at the time, many feel that they have sacrificed something of themselves when they wake up in the morning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-18-2015, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T17:20:29-07:00","id":560015,"title":"","content":"Okay, think I'm gonna leave the Courts alone now that I have Approaches and go back to the Story and Bulwark, figure out the details. First things first, unravel together the Rose Gate, the Treasure Room of Diana, and Grandmother's House from The Path and reweave them into something for Paris. I'll probably figure out the Wayward(Oh hey Hedge essay I haven't finished, what are you doing here?) alongside it.<br /> <br /> <i>Give me feedback on the Rose Courts. I'm starving for feedback.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-18-2015, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T18:00:50-07:00","id":560050,"title":"","content":"I'm looking 