ive and precious quality known only as &quot;Game.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-18-2015, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T21:28:44-07:00","id":560350,"title":"","content":"This went some places and I like all of them.<br /> <br /> Also: awesome job on this. I liked 1e Changeling pretty play, but ranked it rather below Mage. Then Demon, Werewolf, and most recently Beast. But I think that's about to change. This (perhaps what I perceive as) new focus on the narrative metaphysics of the setting has my interest meter pegging out. <br /> <br /> Please, please spoil Pledges soon. The one area of Changling that drove me insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T21:39:08-07:00","id":560357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=560350#post560350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This went some places and I like all of them.<br /> <br /> Also: awesome job on this. I liked 1e Changeling pretty play, but ranked it rather below Mage. Then Demon, Werewolf, and most recently Beast. But I think that's about to change. This (perhaps what I perceive as) new focus on the narrative metaphysics of the setting has my interest meter pegging out.<br /> <br /> Please, please spoil Pledges soon. The one area of Changling that drove me insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will. Pledges got a ground-up overhaul. I think they're keen. Soon!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T21:56:27-07:00","id":560370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=560357#post560357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will. Pledges got a ground-up overhaul. I think they're keen. Soon!</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! They kinda needed it imo. I wait with bated breath. They were somehow my favorite part of Changling in theory and my least favorite part in execution. I'm sure it will be awesome if the spoilers so far are any indication.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T14:58:36-07:00","id":562241,"title":"","content":"While the new system is more flexible from a world building point of view, it's less interesting to me from a player-building-their-PC point of view.<br /> <br /> Part of the fun of making a PC in 1st Edition is choosing combinations of Seeming / Kith / Court to make interesting characters. It was one of the significant choices you had to make for your character. <br /> <br /> The proposed Court system plays very little part in your character's abilities, as far as I can tell. It seems to be primarily window dressing. There's nothing wrong with reducing Court membership to an IC / RP-only component of the character, but it does make the Court-membership decision less significant and interesting, IMO. I find that disappointing.<br /> <br /> LL.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6556-lostlost","name":"LostLost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T16:12:19-07:00","id":562314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=562241#post562241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the new system is more flexible from a world building point of view, it's less interesting to me from a player-building-their-PC point of view.<br /> <br /> Part of the fun of making a PC in 1st Edition is choosing combinations of Seeming / Kith / Court to make interesting characters. It was one of the significant choices you had to make for your character.<br /> <br /> The proposed Court system plays very little part in your character's abilities, as far as I can tell. It seems to be primarily window dressing. There's nothing wrong with reducing Court membership to an IC / RP-only component of the character, but it does make the Court-membership decision less significant and interesting, IMO. I find that disappointing.<br /> <br /> LL.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you be able to elaborate on where you see this happening? Unless I'm missing something from 1e, 2e's take looks like it makes a choice of Court <i>more</i> significant to distinguishing characters.<br /> <br /> I put together a breakdown. Someone please correct me if I'm wildly off-base or missing anything:<br /> <br /> <u>CtL 1e</u><br /> - 2 Court Contracts (devoted to an ideal and an emotion; requires the Court's Mantle, or accessible by any Lost with Court Goodwill)<br /> - Benefit for harvesting Glamour from Court emotion<br /> - Option to purchase Mantle Merit (some social and other bonuses, 2- and 4-dot levels are social-only)<br /> <br /> <u>CtL 2e</u><br /> - 3 Court Contracts (devoted to an ideal and an emotion; also Talespinning*)<br /> - Glamour rules unspecified, but are we <i>really</i> going to assume there's no benefit to harvesting the Court emotion? It's likely just in the section on harvesting Glamour, just like it was in 1e.<br /> - Option to purchase Mantle Merit (some social and other bonuses, 2- and 4-dot levels give Court-specific Goblin Vow and a Personal Approach)<br /> - Court Approaches for Huntsmen and defense against the True Fae (no real analogue to 1e, but hey)<br /> <br /> Even ruling out stuff like the defense against the True Fae and Talespinning for being things that members of all Courts get,** or Approaches for having no analogue in 1e, it looks like 2e's version materially gives everything that 1e's does, plus a Court-specific Goblin Vow. Add to that how the different Approaches seem like they'll have a pretty genuine impact on a Changeling's life,**** and I have trouble seeing where you're coming from on this.<br /> <br /> * And now all I can picture are a number of Beast Changelings working an air delivery service in a period piece.<br /> ** The latter's an assumption, by the by. We don't know how the Talespinning Contract works. Its effects could well vary, giving bonuses to stories that utilize the Court's emotion/ideal.***<br /> *** My personal hunch (plucked from the aether) is that Talespinning can benefit from incorporating thematic elements of a Changeling's Seeming, Kith, Court, etc.<br /> **** We don't yet have mechanics for the Huntsmen and thus lack the full context here, true, but the fluff is pretty emphatic that they're important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Goblin Contract =/= Goblin Vow 06-20-2015, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T20:22:10-07:00","id":562538,"title":"","content":"You mean Goblin Vow Merit, not Goblin Contract, the goblin vows likely tie into the pledge system.<br /> <br /> And I'm curious as to how Talespinning ties into the Courts. Could it affect Mantle somehow? Or maybe its causes visions related to the court. Either way I bet it ties into the courts stories somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T20:31:00-07:00","id":562542,"title":"","content":"Talespinning in 1E was a way for players to set the stage and give some direction to the play in order to claim the story for themselves.<br /> <br /> I imagine 2E will play to similar ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"