e. I don't think there's been any snarling. We'll knit this up just fine.<br /> <br /> o gog i have a disease","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T22:27:22-07:00","id":562637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=562635#post562635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">o gog i have a disease</div> </div> </div> </div>Duel the metaphor of it in the Hedge. Don't forget to duck and weave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T22:36:29-07:00","id":562655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=562314#post562314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you be able to elaborate on where you see this happening?</div> </div> </div> </div>In CtL 1 there are 3 Court contracts (Fleeting, Eternal, and one other) for each major Court, when expansions are included. These three contracts vary quite a bit from each other in exact abilities, allowing for a lot of differences between the Courts. These Contract were generally difficult to get as an outsider, and expensive in terms of XP even if you could get the Goodwill.<br /> <br /> In CtL 2 it appears the proposal is to have 2 generic contracts that vary only by the emotion / story element they influence, plus one more that anyone can have, or that the ST must invent. It sounds like everyone is going to have roughly the same abilities for 2 out of 3 of these at least.<br /> <br /> I have no information on what &quot;Personal Approach&quot; or &quot;Huntsman&quot; are, so I have no way to judge how significant they are. I am new to the forums so possibly I missed this somewhere else?<br /> <br /> The Courts in 1e are a commitment your character makes to an ideal -- one that is individual to the character and independent of any Freehold membership. One could be 'Winter' but not be a member of any Freehold at all, and still be able to find some common ground with another Winter. <br /> <br /> With Courts changed into sects within each freehold, this would no longer seem to be the case. Your character commits to a freehold, and this determines the Court(s) they can choose. If your character isn't in a freehold, can you even have a Court? It seems not. If your character leaves the freehold, or it falters? Poof, no more Court contracts, and no more Mantle abilities?<br /> <br /> What used to be a commitment to a greater ideal, one that guided the character's life, seems to have been reduced to a consequence of which (relatively) small group of Changelings the character chooses to join up with, and what role he has within that small group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6556-lostlost","name":"LostLost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T22:55:48-07:00","id":562666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=562655#post562655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In CtL 1 there are 3 Court contracts (Fleeting, Eternal, and one other) for each major Court, when expansions are included. These three contracts vary quite a bit from each other in exact abilities, allowing for a lot of differences between the Courts. These Contract were generally difficult to get as an outsider, and expensive in terms of XP even if you could get the Goodwill.<br /> <br /> In CtL 2 it appears the proposal is to have 2 generic contracts that vary only by the emotion / story element they influence, plus one more that anyone can have, or that the ST must invent. It sounds like everyone is going to have roughly the same abilities for 2 out of 3 of these at least.<br /> <br /> <b>I have no information on what &quot;Personal Approach&quot; or &quot;Huntsman&quot; are, so I have no way to judge how significant they are. I am new to the forums so possibly I missed this somewhere else?</b><br /> <br /> The Courts in 1e are a commitment your character makes to an ideal -- one that is individual to the character and independent of any Freehold membership. One could be 'Winter' but not be a member of any Freehold at all, and still be able to find some common ground with another Winter.<br /> <br /> With Courts changed into sects within each freehold, this would no longer seem to be the case. Your character commits to a freehold, and this determines the Court(s) they can choose. If your character isn't in a freehold, can you even have a Court? It seems not. If your character leaves the freehold, or it falters? Poof, no more Court contracts, and no more Mantle abilities?<br /> <br /> <b>What used to be a commitment to a greater ideal, one that guided the character's life, seems to have been reduced to a consequence of which (relatively) small group of Changelings the character chooses to join up with, and what role he has within that small group.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>1) We haven't been shown the Huntsmen yet, and the exact ways Approaches work is lost but we know that Approaches are ways to force them to play along to your narrative-force them onto your territory. Considering the Huntsmen are now the more common big threat a Changeling will face, that sort of ability is huge.<br /> <br /> But more on point, instead of holding that against the game, why not wait for more context?<br /> <br /> 2)I'm going to ignore the fact that 'ideal' is incredibly fuzzy here, and instead go for a more pertinent question.<br /> <br /> What makes the the 'ideals' of a universal court system 'greater'?<br /> <br /> Is it the mass of people that support it? Is an ideal only great if people on mass work for it? That seems to miss the point somewhat, particularly with Changeling as an intimate game. An ideal is great and noble because a person believes deeply in it, regardless of how many believe along with him. Is it the symbol set? There are archetypes of power just as potent as the Seasons. What if I want to embody the Sun, the Moon, the Stars, the Infinite Black, the Celestial Spheres singing across the how so big, blue and beautiful? Is the Firebringer lesser than Winter, The Reaper smaller than Autumn(hint: Promethean and Geist respectively disagree). Is it the emotions? What of Desperation, the most potent of all emotions? What of Sorrow, but as a song meant to bring people together rather than a frost to numb the heart?<br /> <br /> It just strikes me as a narrow read(shock that, a narrow read on the internet), to imply that just because each city creates it's own ideals and archetypes and tap into the large narratives that have moved us throughout our lives beyond the rotation of seasons, it's somehow lesser. It seems to ignore that there are endless forms most beautiful to explore, to pretend to, and to evolve into.<br /> <br /> But hey, that's just me.<br /> <br /> As for the Contracts, eh, wait and see, wait and see. You can dismiss a thing you do not know, and call that fair, but you cannot judge it and have it be called the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T22:57:32-07:00","id":562667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=562655#post562655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no information on what &quot;Personal Approach&quot; or &quot;Huntsman&quot; are, so I have no way to judge how significant they are. I am new to the forums so possibly I missed this somewhere else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Approaches are on <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17na4zNJlzOh0D9Qv9pLEcnzXwSnQ8EeZGSpE486BKsc/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Page 4</a>. You'll notice if you go back several pages that this document is posted in the blog entry linked in the first post of this thread that you've decided to participate in.<br /> <br /> Huntsmen are a new antagonist type in Changeling 2e, taking a bit of the narrative pressure off of loyalists and Fae as the main means by which one might be taken back to Faerie. They're discussed a bit on <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/g225t9mnjcwfsxd/Huntsmen%20Chronicle%20Outline.docx\" target=\"_blank\">Page 6 of the outline</a> presented in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline\">this thread</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T12:33:02-07:00","id":563294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=562667#post562667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Approaches are on <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17na4zNJlzOh0D9Qv9pLEcnzXwSnQ8EeZGSpE486BKsc/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Page 4</a>. You'll notice if you go back several pages that this document is posted in the blog entry linked in the first post of this thread that you've decided to participate in.<br /> <br /> Huntsmen are a new antagonist type in Changeling 2e, taking a bit of the narrative pressure off of loyalists and Fae as the main means by which one might be taken back to Faerie. They're discussed a bit on <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/g225t9mnjcwfsxd/Huntsmen%20Chronicle%20Outline.docx\" target=\"_blank\">Page 6 of the outline</a> presented in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline\">this thread</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for that. I totally missed the 'Approaches' section sandwiched in the middle of the example Freehold creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6556-lostlost","name":"LostLost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T12:40:59-07:00","id":563297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=562666#post562666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What makes the the 'ideals' of a universal court system 'greater'?</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant 'greater' in the sense that they are separate from, and not subordinate to, other group <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">allegiances.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6556-lostlost","name":"LostLost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T12:54:46-07:00","id":563312,"title":"","content":"Here's the third of my Gold Mountain Courts, for those who might be interested: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1UELuPD1vB5siNWNkB0oB7D7ZMnLmNv4GBrXKTnN6e38/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Court of the Dome</a>. There are a fair number of similarities between them and the Summer Court, but I've tried to make them more outlaws and vigilantes than soldiers.<br /> <br /> I should probably offer a trigger warning, since the story of Joaquin Murrieta that forms part of the Court's mythology involves a scene of sexual violence. The episode is only briefly touched on here, but it's been a part of the popular story of Murrieta's life since at least 1854 and I feel it would have been remiss of me to gloss over it entirely.<br /> <br /> <br /> And to LostLost, I'd just like to point out that the Seasonal Courts explicitly still exist in Changeling 2e, and sound like they're still going to be a widespread tradition, at least in parts of the Western World where the cycle of four seasons is a major fact of life. I'm personally excited about the new system not just because I love to do this kind of world-building, but also because I live in a part of the world where we don't really have pronounced seasonal changes in the way that they're experienced in, say, Northern Europe. The imagery of the Seasonal Courts doesn't seem all that appropriate in a place where it never snows, the onset of summer is marked by fog rather than sunshine, and so many of the trees are evergreen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-21-2015, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T15:08:42-07:00","id":563434,"title":"","content":"Currently thinking up more on the Freehold based around the Severn Valley... Based on the Welsh side, it's Story is one of rebellion against oppression, stemming from the Romans and going through to various skirmishes against the English and the growth of the Industrial Revolution, a story of when the underdog puts effort in, big things can happen. That's the general idea anyway, it needs some fine tuning and I'm still considering the Bulwark and Emotions. That I'm setting the Freehold in Campbell Country for Mythos shenanigans and crossover potential may have some add to the idea as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T15:16:26-07:00","id":563438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=563297#post563297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant 'greater' in the sense that they are separate from, and not subordinate to, other group <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">allegiances.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay.<br /> <br /> The ideals that make up a freehold are still transcendantly larger than the cities themselves-Mantle 5 Courtiers are living archetypes, and characters of any Mantle are still recognizable as living for their ideal-a Brass Courtier will be seen for their Faith rather quickly, even in a Seasonal Court. Freeholds evoking them just tie a universal and timeless idea down and give it a place to live. Think of ancient city-states where each one stood in for a deity within a pantheon, and you've more or less got it.<br /> <br /> And again, it's not like the Seasonal Court is gone, nor is it mandatory for players to use Court Creation to build their city. The Court Creation system is immensely flexible, allowing the fanbase to make the World of Darkness how they want. You want the Seasonal Courts to be the dominant western power of Changelings to facilitate your sense of keeping the ideals up? You can do that. I don't even think that's a bad option, since it opens the doors more easily for global-tier Changeling games. Want to make your own freehold to reflect how you and your friends deal with trauma? That works too.<br /> <br /> As I mentioned in another thread, you're losing nothing and gaining more options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T15:31:56-07:00","id":563442,"title":"","content":"I want to get something out there: I <i>fucking love</i> the Seasonal Courts. THey are some of my favorite organizations within the New World of Darkness. I love how rich and detailed and imemrsive they are, I really dig the power of that archetype, the feel of it.<br /> <br /> For contrast, I am pleased so far with what I've done with the Rose Courts. I started out wanting to build from two stories that play with a dynamic and set of ideas I really like, and along the way I made courts that ended up kind of revolving around ways I've been throughout my life and the things I learned from them-The White and Black Rose, in particular, speak to some pertinent points in my life, and the Golden, Red, and Blue Rose are right behind them. I'm really proud of what I've done so far and I want to keep building them, and I hope I can convince my playgroup to use it.<br /> <br /> But when I play CtL 2, I really want to play the Seasonal Courts, above and beyond even my own creation that I adore. Because I love them that much.<br /> <br /> But here's the thing. In 1st Edition, that was the norm. Playing outside of the Seasonal Courts involved a lot of work, and it didn't always work neatly, because the support was lacking. Players who wanted to go beyond were tossed into the sea. If you liked them, that was fine, but from day one of Changeling's release(and I should know, I was on the White Wolf Forums for it) people have been trying to build new courts and struggling with the lack of help.<br /> <br /> In 2nd Edition, that's no longer the case. Now there's a clear model for anyone wanting to go and explore their own ideas, and all the while the Seasonal Courts are still there, and from what I've heard, they are in many ways better than ever. Now there's no confinement. People can tell the stories they want to tell, and that's always a good thing.<br /> <br /> That's my opinion though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T15:35:22-07:00","id":563445,"title":"","content":"I am a shameless Autumn Court fanboy, and I agree 100%.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T18:13:56-07:00","id":563595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=563438#post563438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I mentioned in another thread, you're losing nothing and gaining more options.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do actually agree with LostLost in part, though. I'm not sold on the courts being tied to a freehold (because that does feel a little narratively constraining) but the rest of it looks so amazing in scope I'll suspend judgement until I see how it all fits together.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T18:26:10-07:00","id":563603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=563595#post563595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do actually agree with LostLost in part, though. I'm not sold on the courts being tied to a freehold (because that does feel a little narratively constraining) but the rest of it looks so amazing in scope I'll suspend judgement until I see how it all fits together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Joys of the Storyteller System being a toolbox-<i>you don't have to run it that way</i>.<br /> <br /> I don't know how much city hopping people do. It seems to me like people mostly play in one, and therefore the games go for that sort of style(See the Five Cities in CtL's outline). But from what I've read and from what I've heard, there's no reason to assume that court system is only local, or even regional. Changeling is bringing in a butt-ton of flexibility(to an already really flexible game), so while the focus is on the intimate, it's open enough that you can posit global power court-systems(or even cosmic) and have that still gel with the rest of the game. And, remember, this is coming from the guy who hears more than most.<br /> <br /> So I get the idea of the complaint, but speaking as someone who has a broader eye on it all, it's a moot point in execution.<br /> <br /> Now that said, I like the localness. Changeling is a very intimate game, and I think tightening the stories inward rather than outward is a good thing. I've said as much to Dave before, so the focus is pleasing to me. But it's not a debilitating focus in the same way 1E was.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, maybe it's just my conception of the relation of the two ideas, but when I play Changeling, I go looking for home, not ideals. The big, sweeping things will come in anyways, I like having personal spaces that have things that no one else does. I'll find the big ideas in there, not in a global system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-21-2015, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T18:35:01-07:00","id":563614,"title":"","content":"You have no idea how many times I've had arguments about the directional/diurnal/celestial courts being allowed or a thing simply because the book presents them as non-standard.<br /> <br /> Baseline expectations are important too. There's always a degree of 'the book says this, so it works this way' and trying to break out of that with a lot of people is a big source of friction. So, in essence I'm just worried that the 'word of god' tying Courts to a Freehold will mean that for 2E, Courts will always be tied to a Freehold.<br /> <br /> Like what else I said, the freeform creation is amazing and really exciting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 06-21-2015, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T18:47:59-07:00","id":563625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=563614#post563614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have no idea how many times I've had arguments about the directional/diurnal/celestial courts being allowed or a thing simply because the book presents them as non-standard.<br /> <br /> Baseline expectations are important too. There's always a degree of 'the book says this, so it works this way' and trying to break out of that with a lot of people is a big source of friction.</div> </div> </div> </div>THis design more or less explicitly kills the &quot;but it's non-standard&quot; argument, which has been a much bigger issue than the regional/global divide.<br /> <br /> That said, the far extending courts have an implicit presence. In chatting with folks about it, I feel I can mention that the Seasonal Courts are still a thing a lot of Europe and North America use, for instance. Hell, Toronto sort of points at this with the Silver Court being a recent consolidation of the Seasonal(and Seelie) Courts. But I can see the concern...<br /> <br /> though again, knowing play groups as I do, I imagine a common thing said at tables <i>will</i> be &quot;Hey, y'all just wanna run with the Seasons?&quot;, which more or less obviates the point for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T19:04:26-07:00","id":563629,"title":"","content":"After reading through the rough draft I can honestly say that this is the kind of thing that the 2nd edition books are doing right. you can use what ever you want when ever you want where ever want and make it feel organic. want to use the seasonal courts from first edition? sure go ahead. the seelie/unseelie courts of changeling: the dreaming, why not? the game will literally change its self to fit your taste without being obtrusive. my only question is, what happens if a Courtless changeling wins the contest? does that break the bullwork or does the wyrd let it happen with out much fuss?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T19:08:56-07:00","id":563638,"title":"","content":"Courtless characters are in a bit of a bind as is, yeah.<br /> <br /> Funnily enough, my first thought is that'll make for great supplement fodder. But I imagine it'll be a problem for a complete core, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T20:12:04-07:00","id":563670,"title":"","content":"So getting back to actual court creation, specifically for the Rose Courts, you know what I just realized <i>also</i> has a Maiden/Wild One/Woodsman connotation, as well as utterly breaks the narrative, and implies a setting for the Maison du Regret(Rose Gate/Treasure Hold of Diana/Grandmother's House)*, and in fact becomes even more interesting based on the number of real facts that influenced the writing of the fiction?<br /> <br /> Phantom of the Opera. <br /> <br /> This just got more awesome.<br /> <br /> *The Palais Garnier is the 'porch', 'opening hallway', and 'waiting room' of the Maison du Regret.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T22:28:49-07:00","id":563737,"title":"","content":"The biggest issue I had with the Seasonal Courts is that while they're great for some parts of the world, they're useless for a fair chunk. In Southern California the &quot;seasons&quot; are 3 to 5 years of dry and half a year of flooding. In Hawaii, Thailand, Philippines, Okinawa, &amp;c, it's Monsoon season and Not-monsoon season. Canada? Always moose season.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T23:07:45-07:00","id":563752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=563737#post563737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest issue I had with the Seasonal Courts is that while they're great for some parts of the world, they're useless for a fair chunk. In Southern California the &quot;seasons&quot; are 3 to 5 years of dry and half a year of flooding. In Hawaii, Thailand, Philippines, Okinawa, &amp;c, it's Monsoon season and Not-monsoon season. Canada? Always moose season.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just treat Seasonal Courts as major power in Europe and Europe-centric colonies, because of their Roman roots. But I agree the problem with &quot;foreign places&quot; to it's usage - in Poland, I envision that half country would be under Seasonal Courts ( German occupation of few centuries and more &quot;Western&quot; culture in there ) and other half under Courts of Day and Night ( even if I'm not sure they are good Slavic faith representation ).<br /> <br /> For example, mine home city of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lublin\" target=\"_blank\">Lublin</a> would probably have <b>both</b> Seasonal and Day/Night Courts. But I must agree, I have a large problem of Tale that would work with this two groups of Courts then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-22-2015, 02:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T01:59:05-07:00","id":563818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/551489-court-creation?p=563737#post563737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Canada? Always moose season.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey! Idea for an alternative 'Seasonal' system - a wide-ranging group of small towns forming a freehold, and the courts based around different Hunting Seasons!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T02:17:33-07:00","id":563854,"title":"","content":"Been thinking of a court write-up for Budapest. It's not my city, but it is the capital of my country (Hungary) and has a history of being taken over by other empires. Been thinking of a Turkish court, a Habsburg court and a medieval Hungarian court as the major ones, with other courts based on history of the country as well. Bulwark would probably be either playing out sieges of the city, with the defendant being last year's monarch and the attacker being one court who jumped through the right hoops. Will need to research a lot for it, and not sure if historic courts are the right ones here, but seems like a fun idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T04:07:28-07:00","id":563944,"title":"","content":"I think Budapest is going to be one of the cities in the Changeling 2e Corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T05:08:37-07:00","id":564007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-cate